9e2ca48a-9cff-4400-8a45-2325fa04c8d1	321e1167-db92-4f4f-b41c-a6430e8b0c64	10	The Great Rainbow Jungle Party	A collaborative, high-energy sensory painting adventure where children work together on a giant floor canvas to design and paint a vibrant, colorful playground for a herd of toy animals.	{"AgeMax": 5, "AgeMin": 3, "Create": "A giant, multi-textured collaborative jungle mural painted with vibrant washable paints, rollers, sponges, and colorful animal footprints stamped directly onto the canvas.", "Together": "A small group of 3 to 4 children gather around a massive sheet of paper taped to the floor, sharing paint trays, trading toy animals, and deciding together where to paint rivers, trees, and play zones.", "Challenge": "Can we work together to paint a giant, magical rainbow jungle where all of our animal friends can splash, play, and leave colorful paint tracks?", "Materials": ["Giant roll of white butcher paper", "Painter's tape", "Assorted plastic toy animals (elephants, giraffes, lions, zebras)", "Vibrant washable tempera paints or liquid watercolors", "Shallow paint trays for dipping animal feet", "Sponge rollers and textured stampers", "Chubby paintbrushes", "Art smocks for each child"], "Reflection": "Gathering around the edge of the finished giant canvas to share: 'Where is your animal's favorite spot in our new jungle? Who helped you build that part?'", "ChildChoice": "Children choose which plastic animals join the party, which bright colors to paint with, and whether they want to paint with brushes, rollers, or use the toy animals' feet as playful stamps.", "Environment": "Indoor / Outdoor", "MagicMoment": "When two children dip their toy animals' feet in different colors and make them 'dance' together across the paper, laughing as the colors mix to form brand-new colorful tracks.", "GroupSizeMax": 10, "GroupSizeMin": 4, "Accomplishment": "Successfully co-creating a giant, room-sized masterpiece and expressing pride in the shared stories they created through their animals' playful interactions.", "TeacherGuidance": "Secure a very large sheet of butcher paper to the floor using painter's tape. Place shallow trays of bright, washable tempera paints or liquid watercolors around the border. Provide a basket of plastic jungle animals and various playful painting tools (sponges, rollers, chubby brushes). Act as a playful narrator during the experience, prompting collaborative play ('Oh look, the zebra wants to swim in a blue river! Who can help paint a river for them?'). Encourage children to share paint trays and guide them in blending colors together."}	Draft Saved	df5d8828-f7cb-4250-9cd1-dba1d787d531	2026-10-05 23:33:35.989311+00
9cbfda23-e3d7-44f2-9930-4a7763bccdc1	321e1167-db92-4f4f-b41c-a6430e8b0c64	11	The Wobbly-Wiggle Rainbow Jungle Party!	An active, high-energy sensory painting adventure where children transform into jungle explorers, guiding toy animals to stomp, slide, splash, and wiggle across a giant floor canvas to build a colorful, noisy, and beautifully messy playground.	{"AgeMax": 5, "AgeMin": 3, "Create": "A massive, vibrant floor mural bursting with overlapping rainbow tracks, silly 'splat' patterns, swirly slide-trails, and sensory textures created entirely by dancing and spinning painted toy animals.", "Together": "A small group of children gather around a giant paper canvas on the floor, giggling as they mimic animal sounds, slide their toys through gooey paint, and cooperate to make their animals play, leap, and dance together.", "Challenge": "Can we help our toy animals do a wobbly-wiggle dance, splash in magical paint puddles, and make the most colorful, noisy jungle playground ever?", "Materials": ["A giant roll of butcher paper (6-8 feet long)", "Painter's tape (to secure paper to the floor)", "Washable tempera paints in bright neon and primary colors", "Shallow trays (labeled as 'Paint Puddles')", "A basket of plastic toy jungle animals (elephants, lions, giraffes, frogs, etc.)", "Silly textured rollers (labeled as 'Slither Rollers')", "Splat sponges shaped like leaves or clouds", "Chubby paintbrushes (labeled as 'Tickle Wands')", "Wet wipes and a shallow tub of soapy water (labeled as the 'Jungle Bath')"], "Reflection": "Whispering or roaring like their animals to share: 'What was your animal's favorite silly move? Who did your animal splash or dance with today?'", "ChildChoice": "Children choose their toy animal avatar, select their favorite 'puddle' colors, invent their animal's signature silly move (like the 'Hippopotamus Hop' or 'Slithery Slide'), and decide which parts of the jungle to explore.", "Environment": "Indoor / Outdoor", "MagicMoment": "When two children bump their painted toy animals together, make a silly 'Boing!' sound effect, and watch in delight as their paint tracks merge into a brand-new swirly color.", "GroupSizeMax": 10, "GroupSizeMin": 4, "Accomplishment": "Proudly touring the wild, messy canvas and sharing the imaginary, funny stories of how their animals met, danced, and splashed together.", "ExecutionGuide": {"Ask": "", "Try": "", "Watch": "", "Phases": [], "Safety": [], "Closing": "", "Extensions": [], "Adaptations": [], "Preparation": [], "MaterialSetup": [], "EnvironmentSetup": [], "TeacherIntroduction": "", "LittleMomentOpportunity": "", "SuggestedDurationMinutes": 25}, "TeacherGuidance": "Transform into the 'Chief Jungle Guide'! Frame the paint trays as 'magical mud puddles' and the brushes as 'tickle wands'. Instead of giving dry instructions, invite children to make animal noises and physically act out the movements of their toys. Keep the atmosphere dynamic and lighthearted, encouraging children to move around the paper, share paint puddles, and collaborate on silly challenges like 'making a giant rainbow slide.'"}	Draft Saved	df5d8828-f7cb-4250-9cd1-dba1d787d531	2026-10-06 00:12:32.910444+00
e4e57738-65d7-481b-bdd8-9da7a5ed5292	c6544348-31d9-491b-bc55-9020089ce1ad	11	Splashtastic Color Wizards: The Fizzy Flower Rescue	Children become magical Color Wizards working in pairs to build tall block towers (stems) and bring giant coffee-filter flowers to life with vibrant, fizzy watercolor potions!	{"AgeMax": 5, "AgeMin": 3, "Create": "A collaborative 3D flower garden featuring block towers topped with beautifully blended, fizzy watercolor coffee-filter flowers.", "Together": "Working in wizard duos to co-construct block towers, share magic potion cups, and take turns dripping vibrant colors.", "Challenge": "Can you and your partner build a sturdy block tower and splash magic colors to make your flower bloom?", "Materials": ["Wooden building blocks", "Coffee filters cut into flower shapes", "Pipettes or eye droppers", "Vibrant liquid watercolors (Red, Blue, Yellow)", "Baking soda (sprinkled lightly on filters for fizz)", "White vinegar (mixed with watercolors in cups)", "Water trays or plastic trays (to catch drips)", "Plastic cups"], "Reflection": "Giggling together while sharing what their magic flowers smell or feel like, and celebrating how they helped each other build the tallest towers.", "ChildChoice": "Choosing block shapes, selecting and mixing custom potion colors, and deciding whether to drip, splash, or fizz their flowers using pipettes or spray bottles.", "Environment": "Indoor / Outdoor", "MagicMoment": "The eyes-wide-open wonder when the bright watercolors hit the coffee filters on top of their towers, spreading and blending like real blooming magic!", "GroupSizeMax": 10, "GroupSizeMin": 4, "Accomplishment": "Standing back to admire a giant, shared 3D fantasy garden created through teamwork, laughter, and messy exploration.", "ExecutionGuide": {"Ask": "What kind of magic powers does your orange and purple flower have, and how did you and your partner invent that color?", "Try": "If a child is hesitant to touch the wet filters, try giving them a plastic spray bottle or a paintbrush to apply the potion from a comfortable distance.", "Watch": "Watch how children negotiate sharing the pipettes and blocks, and look for moments of shared joy when the fizzy chemical reaction occurs.", "Phases": [{"Name": "The Wizard Alliance", "ChildrenDo": "Find a wizard partner, choose their magical building blocks, and cooperatively build a tower 'stem' inside their tray.", "TeacherDoes": "Guides children into pairs using fun wizard pairing games, hands out blocks, and prompts them to design strong towers together.", "DurationMinutes": 5}, {"Name": "Potion Brewing & Blooming", "ChildrenDo": "Carefully place their coffee-filter flower on top of their block tower. Use pipettes to collect 'magic potion' (colored vinegar) and drip it onto the flower, watching it fizz and blend.", "TeacherDoes": "Enthusiastically narrates the chemical reactions ('Look at that fizz!'), encourages children to share colors, and helps stabilize towers if they wobble.", "DurationMinutes": 12}, {"Name": "The Giant Garden Tour", "ChildrenDo": "Walk around the room with their partner, admiring other wizards' creations, and sharing how they made their colors.", "TeacherDoes": "Leads a playful 'garden walk', pointing out the unique colors, structures, and collaborative efforts of each duo.", "DurationMinutes": 4}, {"Name": "Wizard Cleanup Play", "ChildrenDo": "Use sponges to 'suck up' leftover magic potion from the trays, squeezing it into a central bucket, and helping stack the blocks.", "TeacherDoes": "Turns cleanup into a game of 'Magic Sponge Tag' to keep the playful energy alive while tidying up.", "DurationMinutes": 4}], "Safety": ["Ensure children do not rub eyes after touching the vinegar/baking soda mixtures.", "Keep towels nearby to quickly wipe up any wet spills on the floor to prevent slipping."], "Closing": "Fantastic wizardry, everyone! Our magic garden is fully charged with color! Wave your hands and say: 'Hocus Pocus, fizzy-flow, watch our beautiful garden glow!'", "Extensions": ["Once dry, tape the colorful coffee-filter flowers to the classroom windows to create a 'stained-glass magic garden' that glows in the sunlight."], "Adaptations": ["For children with fine-motor challenges, swap the small pipettes for squeeze bottles or turkey basters which are easier to grasp."], "Preparation": ["Pre-cut coffee filters into fun flower shapes.", "Lightly dust the dry coffee filters with a thin layer of baking soda.", "Mix liquid watercolors with a splash of white vinegar in plastic cups (this creates the fizzy magic reaction)."], "MaterialSetup": ["Place baskets of blocks near the trays.", "Set out pipettes, cups of colorful liquids, and the baking-soda-dusted coffee filter flowers on small trays for each pair."], "EnvironmentSetup": ["Arrange low tables or floor areas with large plastic trays to contain the block building and wet messes.", "Create 'Wizard Potion Stations' where cups of colored vinegar-water are easily accessible."], "TeacherIntroduction": "Welcome, apprentice Color Wizards! Oh no, the forest has lost its sparkle! We need to work in wizarding duos to build giant wooden flower stems and brew magical fizzy potions to make these sleeping flowers bloom again. Are you ready to splash some magic?", "LittleMomentOpportunity": "Catch the moment two children laugh together as their colors bleed into each other on the filter, creating a brand new color they didn't expect.", "SuggestedDurationMinutes": 25}, "TeacherGuidance": "Adopt a playful 'Head Wizard' persona! Instead of focusing on neatness, encourage mess, experimentation, and dramatic play. Help partners coordinate by giving them silly cooperative challenges, like 'Can you place a block at the exact same time?' or 'Mix your potions together to see what new magic you create!'"}	Draft Saved	df5d8828-f7cb-4250-9cd1-dba1d787d531	2026-10-07 21:32:25.422267+00
