771b926e-b7e9-45f7-b776-efb2166a0201	a7409952-18ab-47e0-a7ab-a5b53426343f	7	The Wiggle-Wobble Clay Monster Party	Children wake up sleeping lumps of clay with silly tickles and splats, then transform them into goofy, wiggly monster friends using shaky googly eyes, wiggly pipe cleaners, and fluffy tickle-feathers.	{"AgeMax": 3, "AgeMin": 2, "Create": "Pinch a goofy nose, press in tons of googly eyes, add bouncy zig-zag pipe cleaner legs, and give your monster a fluffy feather tail for tickling.", "Together": "Let's pat, squeeze, and gently splat our clay on the table! We'll tickle the clay to 'wake it up' and make funny yawning noises together.", "Challenge": "Can you make a super silly, wiggly clay monster that loves to dance and make funny noises?", "Materials": ["Brightly colored playdough or air-dry clay", "Assorted sizes of googly eyes", "Colorful pipe cleaners (some pre-bent into zig-zags)", "Fluffy craft feathers", "Soft mini pom-poms for silly noses", "Small plastic cups (to hide the craft parts under)"], "Reflection": "Show me your monster's favorite dance move! What silly sound does it make when you tickle its nose?", "ChildChoice": "Deciding how many eyes to stack, bending pipe cleaners into wild shapes, and inventing their monster's signature silly voice and dance move.", "Environment": "Indoor / Outdoor", "MagicMoment": "When a child tickles their finished monster's tummy with a feather and lets out a huge, shared giggle as they act out the monster's funny voice.", "GroupSizeMax": 10, "GroupSizeMin": 4, "Accomplishment": "Hosting a wild 'Monster Dance Party' on the table, making all our creations wiggle, shake, and shout silly words together.", "ExecutionGuide": {"Ask": "What is your monster's name? Does it make a squeaky sound or a roaring sound when it wiggles?", "Try": "If a monster's wiggly leg falls off, make a dramatic 'Oh no!' sound, poke a deep finger hole into the clay together, and pinch it tight while saying '1, 2, 3, stick!'", "Watch": "Watch for children giggling and engaging in pretend play. Keep an eye out to make sure small googly eyes and pom-poms stay on the trays and out of mouths.", "Phases": [{"Name": "Wake Up & Splat!", "ChildrenDo": "Tickle, squeeze, and gently splat their clay on the tray to warm it up, making silly 'wake up' sounds.", "TeacherDoes": "Lead the stretching and squeezing with funny sound effects like 'streeeetch' and 'splat!'.", "DurationMinutes": 6}, {"Name": "The Magic Reveal", "ChildrenDo": "Lift up their surprise cups to discover the eyes, wiggly pipe cleaners, and feathers hidden underneath.", "TeacherDoes": "Gasp in excitement and encourage children to name the colorful treasures they found under their 'surprise hats'.", "DurationMinutes": 4}, {"Name": "Build a Goofy Friend", "ChildrenDo": "Press eyes, zig-zag legs, and feathers into their clay to build a silly monster face and body.", "TeacherDoes": "Circulate and make funny 'boop' and 'pop' noises as kids press items into the clay.", "DurationMinutes": 10}, {"Name": "The Monster Dance Party!", "ChildrenDo": "Bounce their finished monsters on the table dance floor, making them wiggle and make silly noises.", "TeacherDoes": "Play some upbeat, playful background music and narrate the funny dance moves the monsters are doing.", "DurationMinutes": 5}], "Safety": ["Ensure pipe cleaner ends are tucked or folded so they are not sharp.", "Actively supervise to prevent any mouthing of the small googly eyes or pom-poms."], "Closing": "Let's tuck our tired monsters into their trays for a nap. Let's whisper, 'Goodnight, silly monsters, thank you for dancing with us!'", "Extensions": ["Create a simple 'Monster Freeze Dance' game where children freeze their clay monsters when the music stops.", "Provide cardboard boxes as 'monster cars' to slide them around the room."], "Adaptations": ["For younger toddlers: Focus purely on poking big craft sticks and giant eyes into the clay to make 'peek-a-boo' faces.", "For older children: Challenge them to make a monster that can balance on one giant wiggly leg."], "Preparation": ["Roll the clay into round 'sleeping' balls.", "Bend several pipe cleaners into zig-zags and spirals.", "Hide the eyes, feathers, and pom-poms under plastic cups on each tray like secret surprise hats."], "MaterialSetup": ["Place a 'sleeping' ball of clay on each tray.", "Place the upside-down surprise cups next to the clay."], "EnvironmentSetup": ["Create a 'Monster Dance Floor' by taping a bright sheet of paper in the center of the table.", "Set up individual trays for each child to contain the playdough splats."], "TeacherIntroduction": "Shh... look! Our clay balls are fast asleep! On the count of three, let's give them a gentle tickle and shout 'WAKE UP, CLAY!' One, two, three... WAKE UP!", "LittleMomentOpportunity": "When a child puts an eye in a weird place like the bottom of the clay, dramatically pretend the monster is looking at your toes and giggle together about its 'toe-vision'.", "SuggestedDurationMinutes": 25}, "TeacherGuidance": "Keep the energy high and full of pretend play. Use your voice to bring the clay to life—giggle when you touch it, make 'boop' sounds when adding eyes, and encourage children to talk to their monsters. Focus on the joy of creation rather than making a perfect figure."}	Draft Saved	df5d8828-f7cb-4250-9cd1-dba1d787d531	2026-10-07 22:54:41.910702+00
1d0d0745-c1d1-430e-a247-3e4210f87450	f0fa25a2-84a1-4eed-bd40-1d8d260bdc64	21	Wobbly Towers & Secret Toy Hideouts		{"AgeMax": 3, "AgeMin": 2, "Create": "Building a wacky, gravity-defying tower using blocks and cardboard tubes, or wrapping colorful fabrics to make a secret, cozy hideout for a tiny toy animal friend!", "Together": "A busy squad of tiny architects plotting secret designs, passing blocks with funny sound effects, and high-fiving as they save each other's towers from tumbling!", "Challenge": "Cooperating with a buddy to build a giant, wobbly tower or a secret castle for a tiny toy animal!", "Materials": ["Blocks", "Paper", "Cups", "Water tray"], "Reflection": "Sharing a silly 'wobble dance' together to celebrate how you helped each other save the tumbling towers!", "ChildChoice": "Choosing which silly toy animal needs a home (like a sleepy dinosaur or a dancing kitten) and deciding if their hideout needs a slide, a secret trapdoor, or googly-eye windows!", "Environment": "Indoor", "MagicMoment": "The breathless gasps and eruption of giggles when the wobbly tower sways, nearly falls, and is saved at the very last second by a teammate's quick hand!", "GroupSizeMax": 10, "GroupSizeMin": 4, "Accomplishment": "The proud grin of standing back to admire a wonderfully wacky, wobbly tower, and the joy of sharing a silly 'we did it!' high-five with a teammate!", "ExecutionGuide": {"Ask": "", "Try": "", "Watch": "", "Phases": [], "Safety": [], "Closing": "", "Extensions": [], "Adaptations": [], "Preparation": [], "MaterialSetup": [], "EnvironmentSetup": [], "TeacherIntroduction": "", "LittleMomentOpportunity": "", "SuggestedDurationMinutes": 25}, "TeacherGuidance": "Channel your inner playful partner! Walk around testing the wobbly towers by gently blowing on them like a silly, warm breeze, and ask imaginative questions in a playful whisper, like, 'Does your dancing kitten need a marshmallow slide or a secret trampoline in their hideout?'"}	Draft Saved	df5d8828-f7cb-4250-9cd1-dba1d787d531	2026-10-07 22:55:47.768214+00
65814402-ea15-4b38-abea-aba4dad8ceb3	f0fa25a2-84a1-4eed-bd40-1d8d260bdc64	22	Wobbly Towers & Secret Toy Hideouts		{"AgeMax": 3, "AgeMin": 2, "Create": "Building a wacky, gravity-defying tower using blocks and cardboard tubes, or wrapping colorful fabrics to make a secret, cozy hideout for a tiny toy animal friend!", "Together": "A busy squad of tiny architects plotting secret designs, passing blocks with funny sound effects, and high-fiving as they save each other's towers from tumbling!", "Challenge": "Cooperating with a buddy to build a giant, wobbly tower or a secret castle for a tiny toy animal!", "Materials": ["Blocks", "Paper", "Cups", "Water tray"], "Reflection": "Sharing a silly 'wobble dance' together to celebrate how you helped each other save the tumbling towers!", "ChildChoice": "Choosing which silly toy animal needs a home (like a sleepy dinosaur or a dancing kitten) and deciding if their hideout needs a slide, a secret trapdoor, or googly-eye windows!", "Environment": "Indoor", "MagicMoment": "The breathless gasps and eruption of giggles when the wobbly tower sways, nearly falls, and is saved at the very last second by a teammate's quick hand!", "GroupSizeMax": 10, "GroupSizeMin": 4, "Accomplishment": "The proud grin of standing back to admire a wonderfully wacky, wobbly tower, and the joy of sharing a silly 'we did it!' high-five with a teammate!", "ExecutionGuide": {"Ask": "", "Try": "", "Watch": "", "Phases": [], "Safety": [], "Closing": "", "Extensions": [], "Adaptations": [], "Preparation": [], "MaterialSetup": [], "EnvironmentSetup": [], "TeacherIntroduction": "", "LittleMomentOpportunity": "", "SuggestedDurationMinutes": 25}, "TeacherGuidance": "Channel your inner playful partner! Walk around testing the wobbly towers by gently blowing on them like a silly, warm breeze, and ask imaginative questions in a playful whisper, like, 'Does your dancing kitten need a marshmallow slide or a secret trampoline in their hideout?'"}	Draft Saved	df5d8828-f7cb-4250-9cd1-dba1d787d531	2026-10-07 22:55:50.293447+00
8caa9b70-36f1-41fb-98de-d04e97938eb6	f0fa25a2-84a1-4eed-bd40-1d8d260bdc64	23	Wobbly Towers & Secret Toy Hideouts		{"AgeMax": 3, "AgeMin": 2, "Create": "Building a wacky, gravity-defying tower using blocks and cardboard tubes, or wrapping colorful fabrics to make a secret, cozy hideout for a tiny toy animal friend!", "Together": "A busy squad of tiny architects plotting secret designs, passing blocks with funny sound effects, and high-fiving as they save each other's towers from tumbling!", "Challenge": "Cooperating with a buddy to build a giant, wobbly tower or a secret castle for a tiny toy animal!", "Materials": ["Blocks", "Paper", "Cups", "Water tray"], "Reflection": "Sharing a silly 'wobble dance' together to celebrate how you helped each other save the tumbling towers!", "ChildChoice": "Choosing which silly toy animal needs a home (like a sleepy dinosaur or a dancing kitten) and deciding if their hideout needs a slide, a secret trapdoor, or googly-eye windows!", "Environment": "Indoor", "MagicMoment": "The breathless gasps and eruption of giggles when the wobbly tower sways, nearly falls, and is saved at the very last second by a teammate's quick hand!", "GroupSizeMax": 10, "GroupSizeMin": 4, "Accomplishment": "The proud grin of standing back to admire a wonderfully wacky, wobbly tower, and the joy of sharing a silly 'we did it!' high-five with a teammate!", "ExecutionGuide": {"Ask": "", "Try": "", "Watch": "", "Phases": [], "Safety": [], "Closing": "", "Extensions": [], "Adaptations": [], "Preparation": [], "MaterialSetup": [], "EnvironmentSetup": [], "TeacherIntroduction": "", "LittleMomentOpportunity": "", "SuggestedDurationMinutes": 25}, "TeacherGuidance": "Channel your inner playful partner! Walk around testing the wobbly towers by gently blowing on them like a silly, warm breeze, and ask imaginative questions in a playful whisper, like, 'Does your dancing kitten need a marshmallow slide or a secret trampoline in their hideout?'"}	Draft Saved	df5d8828-f7cb-4250-9cd1-dba1d787d531	2026-10-07 22:55:51.728758+00
6dde88a8-e95f-4bed-a644-14ef7f18abe8	f0fa25a2-84a1-4eed-bd40-1d8d260bdc64	24	The Great Wobble-O-Saurus & the Wacky, Shakey Towers!	A super playful, giggle-filled building adventure where children work together to build the silliest, most gravity-defying towers for their toy animal buddies, while dodging the friendly 'Wobble-O-Saurus' earthquake!	{"AgeMax": 3, "AgeMin": 2, "Create": "Stacking foam cups, cardboard tubes, and blocks onto a wobbly cushion or tray, and adding funny decorations like googly eyes to make a silly home for their toy animals.", "Together": "A team of giggling builders passing cups with funny sound effects, stacking silly objects, and gasping together as their tower does a wiggly dance!", "Challenge": "Work with a buddy to build a wacky, super-tall tower on a shaky foundation that can survive the silly 'Wobble-O-Saurus' shake!", "Materials": ["Foam cups", "Cardboard tubes", "Soft sponges or cushions (to use as shaky foundations)", "Small plastic toy animals", "Googly eyes on tape", "Feather duster or pool noodle (for the Wobble-O-Saurus)"], "Reflection": "Pretending to be wobbly towers themselves, shaking from side to side, and then collapsing onto the floor in a silly slow-motion melt together!", "ChildChoice": "Choosing their toy animal partner, naming their tower a silly name (like 'Captain Cup-Cake'), and deciding if their building gets a cup-hat, a slide, or a secret trampoline!", "Environment": "Indoor", "MagicMoment": "The hilarious suspense as the teacher pretends to be the 'Wobble-O-Saurus', making funny rumbling noises, while the children quickly strike a funny 'freeze pose' to protect their shaky masterpiece!", "GroupSizeMax": 10, "GroupSizeMin": 4, "Accomplishment": "Doing the 'Wobbly-Wobble Dance of Victory' with your partner when your tower stands tall—or collapses in a glorious cloud of giggles!", "ExecutionGuide": {"Ask": "What silly sound does your tower make when it wiggles? Can you show me your best Wobble-O-Saurus face?", "Try": "Try adding a giant foam cup hat to the very top of your tower to see if it makes it wobble even more!", "Watch": "Look for children who laugh when things fall, and encourage teammates who help each other rebuild with even sillier, wider designs.", "Phases": [{"Name": "Partner Up & Pick a Buddy", "ChildrenDo": "Choose a partner and select a toy animal who needs a 'wacky tower house'. Give the animal a funny voice.", "TeacherDoes": "Help children form pairs and pass out the animal toys with silly sound effects.", "DurationMinutes": 3}, {"Name": "Build the Wiggle-Tower", "ChildrenDo": "Stack cups and tubes on top of the wobbly sponge foundation, making funny 'beep-boop' sounds for every block added.", "TeacherDoes": "Circulate, admire the wacky designs, and suggest adding silly details like 'cup-hats' or googly-eye windows.", "DurationMinutes": 10}, {"Name": "The Wobble-O-Saurus Shake!", "ChildrenDo": "Hold hands or strike a funny 'shield pose' over their tower as the teacher gently taps their wobbly sponge foundation.", "TeacherDoes": "Pretend to be the Wobble-O-Saurus! Make gentle rumbling sounds, gently tap the sponges to make the towers wiggle, and cheer wildly when they tumble.", "DurationMinutes": 5}, {"Name": "Wobble Dance Celebration", "ChildrenDo": "Celebrate their towers (standing or fallen!) by doing a silly, shaky wiggle dance with their partners.", "TeacherDoes": "Lead a high-energy 'Wobble Dance' and help children transition to clean-up.", "DurationMinutes": 2}], "Safety": ["Ensure toy animals are large enough to not be choking hazards.", "Keep building materials lightweight (foam cups, cardboard) so falling structures are completely safe and quiet."], "Closing": "High-five your partner, give your toy animal a cozy squeeze, and let's do one last giant shake-out wobble!", "Extensions": ["Use a flashlight to cast giant 'wobbly monster shadows' of the towers on the classroom wall!", "Add colorful socks to slide over the cardboard tubes to give the towers silly, bright patterns."], "Adaptations": ["For children who get frustrated when towers fall, build directly on the solid floor instead of a sponge foundation to make it sturdy.", "For a quieter experience, use soft dish sponges as the building blocks to make a completely silent, sneaky tower."], "Preparation": ["Gather foam cups, cardboard tubes, and sponges.", "Set up building stations on the rug with plenty of space between pairs."], "MaterialSetup": ["Place a soft sponge or cushion at each station as the 'Wobble Zone' foundation.", "Put baskets of foam cups, tubes, and toy animals within easy reach of each station."], "EnvironmentSetup": ["Clear a wide floor space so children can easily sit in pairs and have room for falling cups to scatter safely."], "TeacherIntroduction": "Oh no! The friendly Wobble-O-Saurus is coming to town, and they love to dance! Can you and your partner build a wacky, super-tall tower for your toy animals that can survive the Great Wobble Dance? Let's build!", "LittleMomentOpportunity": "When a tower inevitably falls, gasp dramatically, fall to the floor in a silly slow-motion melt, and shout 'Boom-shaka-laka!' to turn a collapse into the absolute highlight of the game.", "SuggestedDurationMinutes": 20}, "TeacherGuidance": "Embody the playful Wobble-O-Saurus! Walk around making silly, low rumbling noises, warning children of 'gentle tremors' coming. Use a soft feather duster to gently tickle or blow a 'silly breeze' on their towers. Keep the energy light, dramatic, and focused on the joy of rebuilding together rather than keeping things perfect."}	Draft Saved	df5d8828-f7cb-4250-9cd1-dba1d787d531	2026-10-07 22:56:14.698535+00
e6ea6455-c7ef-4b8b-8245-0abc816064a4	025724ee-46ad-4f3e-b37a-c573ecada70d	3	Silly Splash Island Water Park	A playful water-building adventure where children construct silly islands, wild water slides, and floating splash-zones for toy characters using cups, blocks, and water.	{"AgeMax": 5, "AgeMin": 3, "Create": "Children build splash zones! They stack cups to make water towers, line up blocks as slippery slides, and float cup-boats, letting their toy animals dive, slide, and splash into the water.", "Together": "We gather around the water tray. The teacher introduces some silly toy animals who 'really want to go swimming!' We practice making our best splashing sounds (Whoosh! Splash!) and talk about what rides we want to build for them.", "Challenge": "Can you build a silly splash park with slides, pools, or boats for your toy friends to play on?", "Materials": ["Water tray filled halfway", "Plastic or foam building blocks", "Plastic cups (various sizes)", "Small plastic toy animals or characters", "Sponges and small pitchers for pouring"], "Reflection": "Ask the children: 'What was your toy's favorite ride today? Who made the loudest splash sound? What should we build for our next water park adventure?'", "ChildChoice": "Children choose which toy animal to play with, whether to build a tall slide or a floating boat, and how much splashing and pouring their toy gets to do.", "Environment": "Indoor / Outdoor", "MagicMoment": "The exact second a child slides a toy animal down a wet block ramp and it lands with a satisfying 'splat!' right inside a floating cup!", "GroupSizeMax": 10, "GroupSizeMin": 4, "Accomplishment": "Each child gives their toy animal one giant 'Grand Finale Splash' into their creation while making a loud, silly sound effect!", "ExecutionGuide": {"Ask": "Ask playful questions: 'Is your toy going down the fast slide or taking a relaxing cup-bath? Can we make a rainstorm with this sponge to fill your pool?'", "Try": "Try adding a playful twist if a child is stuck: 'Oh look, this little frog is looking for a floating island! Can you build him a boat using a cup and a block?'", "Watch": "Watch for dramatic play narratives. Note how children use the physical properties of water (buoyancy, pouring, sliding) to fuel their imaginative scenarios with the toys.", "Phases": [{"Name": "Meet the Swimmers", "ChildrenDo": "Choose a toy animal, test how it floats, and splash it in the water while making funny animal noises.", "TeacherDoes": "Hand out toys, encourage silly swimming sounds, and ask children what kind of water ride their toy wants.", "DurationMinutes": 5}, {"Name": "Build the Wild Rides", "ChildrenDo": "Stack blocks to make slides, float cups as hot tubs, and use sponges to rain water down on their toys.", "TeacherDoes": "Playfully narrate the building: 'Wow, Leo's dinosaur is climbing a giant block tower! Look at that splash!'", "DurationMinutes": 12}, {"Name": "The Grand Splash Show", "ChildrenDo": "Show off their favorite ride by sending their toy down the slide or into the pool with a big collective splash.", "TeacherDoes": "Cheer, countdown '3-2-1 Splash!', and celebrate everyone's silly ideas.", "DurationMinutes": 5}, {"Name": "Splash-Free Cleanup", "ChildrenDo": "Squeeze water out of sponges, load toys and blocks into drying baskets, and dry their hands.", "TeacherDoes": "Make cleanup a game by asking children to rescue the toys from the water and tuck them into dry towel beds.", "DurationMinutes": 3}], "Safety": ["Keep the floor dry by having sponges ready to soak up spills.", "Remind children to keep splashing gentle and inside the water tray area."], "Closing": "You built the best water park ever! Our toy friends are so happy and tired from all the sliding and splashing. High-fives for our silly builders!", "Extensions": ["Add plastic funnels or bendy straws to create 'water pipes' and secret slides.", "Give children washable markers to draw swimsuits on plastic toys before they dive in."], "Adaptations": ["For children who dislike getting wet, let them build a dry block-tower 'viewing deck' next to the water for their toy.", "For extra sensory fun, add bubble bath to the water tray for a soapy splash park."], "Preparation": ["Fill the water tray halfway with warm water.", "Gather a basket of plastic blocks, cups, and toy animals next to the tray."], "MaterialSetup": ["Drop a few cups and toys directly in the water to invite immediate play.", "Keep blocks and sponges dry in baskets nearby so kids can choose when to wet them."], "EnvironmentSetup": ["Place the water tray in an easy-to-reach spot.", "Lay down towels or a plastic splash mat underneath to catch wild splashes."], "TeacherIntroduction": "Oh no! Our toy animal friends are so hot and want to go to a wild water park! But there are no rides yet! Can you help me build the silliest splash islands, slides, and pools ever? Let's make some waves!", "LittleMomentOpportunity": "When a child naturally starts making their toy talk or slide down a block, lean in and pretend to be a customer waiting in line for their amazing ride!", "SuggestedDurationMinutes": 25}, "TeacherGuidance": "Keep the energy light and joyful. Act as the play coordinator—narrate the toys' adventures with fun sound effects (Wheee! Splash!) and encourage silly ways to move water, like pouring from high up or making mini waves.", "DevelopmentalGoals": []}	Draft Saved	df5d8828-f7cb-4250-9cd1-dba1d787d531	2026-10-07 23:10:25.737085+00
635e3c33-546a-42a3-b8be-b1770256ba71	025724ee-46ad-4f3e-b37a-c573ecada70d	4	Silly Splash Island Water Park	A playful water-building adventure where children construct silly islands, wild water slides, and floating splash-zones for toy characters using cups, blocks, and water.	{"AgeMax": 5, "AgeMin": 3, "Create": "Children build splash zones! They stack cups to make water towers, line up blocks as slippery slides, and float cup-boats, letting their toy animals dive, slide, and splash into the water.", "Together": "We gather around the water tray. The teacher introduces some silly toy animals who 'really want to go swimming!' We practice making our best splashing sounds (Whoosh! Splash!) and talk about what rides we want to build for them.", "Challenge": "Can you build a silly splash park with slides, pools, or boats for your toy friends to play on?", "Materials": ["Water tray filled halfway", "Plastic or foam building blocks", "Plastic cups (various sizes)", "Small plastic toy animals or characters", "Sponges and small pitchers for pouring"], "Reflection": "Ask the children: 'What was your toy's favorite ride today? Who made the loudest splash sound? What should we build for our next water park adventure?'", "ChildChoice": "Children choose which toy animal to play with, whether to build a tall slide or a floating boat, and how much splashing and pouring their toy gets to do.", "Environment": "Indoor / Outdoor", "MagicMoment": "The exact second a child slides a toy animal down a wet block ramp and it lands with a satisfying 'splat!' right inside a floating cup!", "GroupSizeMax": 10, "GroupSizeMin": 4, "Accomplishment": "Each child gives their toy animal one giant 'Grand Finale Splash' into their creation while making a loud, silly sound effect!", "ExecutionGuide": {"Ask": "Ask playful questions: 'Is your toy going down the fast slide or taking a relaxing cup-bath? Can we make a rainstorm with this sponge to fill your pool?'", "Try": "Try adding a playful twist if a ch