cb208fee-76d9-4406-b620-dae40b3ae507	3a48a470-63cd-492c-ba6f-8dd3032205cf	8	Captain Hippo's Splashy Sailboat Adventure!	A playful origami adventure where children become sea captains! They fold 'magic pocket boats', coat them with 'water-shield' crayons, and launch them on a colorful ocean rescue mission to save toy animal passengers and sail to sponge islands.	{"AgeMax": 4, "AgeMin": 3, "Create": "Scribble-paint the boat with colorful wax armor, place a tiny animal toy passenger inside the fold, and blow through a straw to sail across the blue bubbly ocean to safe sponge islands!", "Together": "We will transform our flat paper into a silly captain's hat, fold up the edges to make a secret cabin, and scribble 'magic armor' with shiny wax crayons to protect our toy passengers from the waves!", "Challenge": "Can you build a magic paper boat that keeps your tiny toy animal dry during a wild windstorm?", "Materials": ["Square origami paper or bright construction paper (12cm x 12cm)", "Chunky wax crayons (magical water shields)", "Shallow plastic trays with 2cm of blue-colored water", "A drop of dish soap (for bubbly waves)", "Silly animal figurines or toy passengers", "Colorful kitchen sponges (to act as 'Sponge Islands')", "Colorful drinking straws (to blow 'wind storms')", "Towels for splash cleanup"], "Reflection": "Where did your animal passenger travel today? How did the magic crayon shield fight off the water monsters?", "ChildChoice": "Children choose their boat's 'magic shield' crayon colors, pick their own animal passenger, select which sponge island to sail to, and name their vessel.", "Environment": "Indoor / Outdoor", "MagicMoment": "The giggles when captains blow through their straws, causing their boats to zoom across the blue bubbly water, and seeing their animal passengers survive the wild ride dry!", "GroupSizeMax": 10, "GroupSizeMin": 4, "Accomplishment": "Successfully building a waterproof vessel that sails across a bubbly sea and completes a rescue mission!", "ExecutionGuide": {"Ask": "Oh no, a giant wave! Can your captain's boat make it to Sponge Island? What sound does your boat make when it zooms?", "Try": "Try sliding your thumb along the fold like a little toy train zooming on a track to make the crease super strong!", "Watch": "Watch for captains who get too excited with the straws and accidentally blow water or submerge their boats. Remind them to blow gently across the top of the sail, not down into the water.", "Phases": [{"Name": "The Magic Hat Fold", "ChildrenDo": "Fold the square corner-to-corner to make a giant taco triangle, then wear it as a silly captain's hat for a second!", "TeacherDoes": "Demonstrates the fold with dramatic flair, helping children make 'strong iron creases' with their thumbs.", "DurationMinutes": 5}, {"Name": "Making the Secret Pocket", "ChildrenDo": "Fold the bottom point up to make a secret pocket (the boat hull) where the passenger will sit.", "TeacherDoes": "Guides them to tuck the fold tightly, pretending to whisper a secret into the boat's pocket.", "DurationMinutes": 5}, {"Name": "Wax Armor Painting", "ChildrenDo": "Scribble fast and furiously with wax crayons to coat the entire bottom of the boat in 'magic water-repelling armor'.", "TeacherDoes": "Plays fast-paced music or makes silly 'scribble sounds' (zip, zap, zoop!) to encourage heavy crayon coating.", "DurationMinutes": 7}, {"Name": "The Great Ocean Rescue", "ChildrenDo": "Put their toy passenger in the pocket, launch the boat in the bubbly blue water, and blow through straws to guide it to a Sponge Island.", "TeacherDoes": "Acts as the wind helper, cheering on the captains and making gentle wave sounds as they sail to safety.", "DurationMinutes": 8}], "Safety": ["Ensure children do not share or inhale through the drinking straws; keep straws single-use and clearly marked.", "Keep towels ready on the floor for immediate cleanup of any splashy puddles."], "Closing": "Have captains dock their boats on towel 'docks', dry off their animal passengers with a cozy towel blanket, and celebrate the successful rescue with a loud pirate cheer: 'Arrr!'", "Extensions": ["Create a 'bubbly storm' by having children gently blow bubbles in the water tray using their straws before sailing.", "Add a target bell or flag on the sponge islands that their boat has to touch to complete the mission."], "Adaptations": ["For younger sailors, use pre-folded boats or thicker waxed patty papers so they can focus entirely on the playful coloring and water play.", "For older captains, add obstacles like floating plastic bottle caps (icebergs) to navigate around."], "Preparation": ["Add a drop of blue food coloring and a tiny squirt of dish soap to shallow trays to make bubbly blue water.", "Float a few colorful sponges in the water to serve as 'islands' for the toy passengers."], "MaterialSetup": ["Place a basket of chunky crayons, square paper, and straws at the dry tables. Keep the bubbly water trays covered with 'fog' (light towels) until launch time."], "EnvironmentSetup": ["Set up 'Port Table' for the dry folding and coloring, and 'The Great Blue Ocean' table for the water play."], "TeacherIntroduction": "Ahoy, brave Captains! Today, a friendly sea monster lost all his animal friends on the Sponge Islands! We need to fold magic pocket boats, paint them with colorful wax armor, and sail them through a giant windstorm to rescue them. Are you ready to sail the Crayon Sea?", "LittleMomentOpportunity": "Taking a photo of a child wearing their paper fold as a silly hat, laughing as they realize they are a real boat captain.", "SuggestedDurationMinutes": 25}, "TeacherGuidance": "Keep the energy high by acting like a playful lighthouse keeper. Encourage silly sound effects (whoosh, splash!) during folding. Model the 'magic shield' crayon scribbling as a fun speed-coloring game where no white spots are left behind!", "DevelopmentalGoals": []}	Draft Saved	df5d8828-f7cb-4250-9cd1-dba1d787d531	2026-10-09 12:05:01.956272+00
