-blanket tuck-in, and doing a giant group 'Wobbly Seaweed Dance' to celebrate their success!", "Extensions": ["Have a 'Bubble Nose-Pop' game where kids try to pop the tallest bubble using only the tip of their nose without touching it with their hands!", "Add a drop of red paint to the sponge islands to watch the blue bubble water magically swirl into purple when they arrive!"], "Adaptations": ["For younger children, pre-fold the boats so they can jump straight into the coloring and bubble-blowing play.", "For older kids, challenge them to build a 'bubble bridge' across the tray using two straws at the same time."], "Preparation": ["Mix water, blue food coloring, and plenty of dish soap in the plastic trays.", "Cut colorful sponges into star, cloud, or heart shapes to act as 'Silly Sponge Islands' and place them inside the trays."], "MaterialSetup": ["Place crayons in bright baskets, stack the square paper, and cover the water trays with colorful towels to make the 'Big Bubble Reveal' exciting."], "EnvironmentSetup": ["Create a 'Silly Shipyard' coloring table with bright decorations and a nearby 'Bubbly Ocean Arena' for the water play trays."], "TeacherIntroduction": "Welcome to the Bubbly Scribble-Ship Circus! I am your Ringleader! A giant, ticklish Bubble Monster is tickling our toes! We need to make shiny, crayon-armored circus boats, grab our squeakiest animal friends, and blow a huge, wobbly shield of blue bubbles to protect them! Who is ready to get silly?", "LittleMomentOpportunity": "The pure joy when a child successfully blows a bubble dome so big that it completely encapsulates their little toy animal passenger, leading to gasps and giggles.", "SuggestedDurationMinutes": 25}, "TeacherGuidance": "Become a cartoon character! Wear a silly hat, use funny sound effects (whoosh, pop, boing), make giant cartoonish facial expressions, and treat every step like an exciting, playful game.", "DevelopmentalGoals": []}	Draft Saved	df5d8828-f7cb-4250-9cd1-dba1d787d531	2026-10-09 13:36:47.231115+00
