e2eb2e7b-d9bd-4c93-be84-0d3c05439acb	b5dd39a8-9b41-4681-9ec8-4a209aa35fcd	3	The Great Underwater Fishy Adventure	Children dive into a world of imagination, crafting colorful, tactile fish friends and designing the magical places where they live, turning their creations into a living story.	{"AgeMax": 5, "AgeMin": 3, "Create": "A collection of whimsical fish characters and their unique, textured underwater worlds.", "Together": "Children work side-by-side, sharing 'underwater' treasures and helping their fish friends visit each other's habitats.", "Challenge": "Can we build a vibrant, textured home for our new fish friends to explore?", "Materials": ["Fish-shaped cutouts", "Sparkly sequins and buttons", "Soft felt scraps", "Textured paper and ribbons", "Washable craft adhesive", "Wooden craft sticks for puppets", "Blue fabric or paper for the 'ocean' base"], "Reflection": "If your fish could talk, what is the first thing it would say about its new home?", "ChildChoice": "Children choose their fish's colors, scales, and the secret spots where their fish likes to hide.", "Environment": "Indoor", "MagicMoment": "Watching a child give their fish a personality and name as they place it into their handmade habitat.", "GroupSizeMax": 6, "GroupSizeMin": 2, "Accomplishment": "Sharing a short, joyful story about their fish's daily adventure with the group.", "ExecutionGuide": {"Ask": "Where does your fish like to hide when it plays hide-and-seek?", "Try": "Try making your fish swim through the air to visit a friend's habitat.", "Watch": "Observe how children use their imaginations to narrate the lives of their fish.", "Phases": [{"Name": "Ocean Discovery", "ChildrenDo": "Explore the 'ocean' table and choose a fish cutout to adopt", "TeacherDoes": "Uses a playful voice to describe the 'underwater' environment", "DurationMinutes": 5}, {"Name": "Building Habitats", "ChildrenDo": "Decorate their fish and create a cozy home using textures and shapes", "TeacherDoes": "Encourages storytelling by asking about the fish's favorite snacks or games", "DurationMinutes": 15}, {"Name": "Fishy Parade", "ChildrenDo": "Bring their fish to visit other habitats and share a quick story", "TeacherDoes": "Facilitates a gentle 'swimming' transition to the sharing circle", "DurationMinutes": 5}], "Safety": ["Monitor the use of small decorative items like buttons", "Ensure all adhesives are non-toxic and child-safe"], "Closing": "Gather in a circle to let all the fish 'swim' together one last time before resting.", "Extensions": ["Create a 'classroom aquarium' display on the wall using all the finished habitats"], "Adaptations": ["Provide pre-glued textured shapes for children who prefer to focus on the story"], "Preparation": ["Create a 'deep sea' area with blue fabric", "Organize materials into 'treasure' trays"], "MaterialSetup": ["Arrange materials in inviting, accessible trays within reach of all children"], "EnvironmentSetup": ["Clear a low table and cover it with blue paper to represent the ocean floor"], "TeacherIntroduction": "Welcome, explorers! Today we are diving deep into the ocean to meet some new fish friends. Let's see what kind of magical homes we can build for them!", "LittleMomentOpportunity": "Celebrate a child who creates a funny or unique feature for their fish, like a glittery hat or a ribbon tail.", "SuggestedDurationMinutes": 25}, "TeacherGuidance": "Set the stage with a playful tone, encouraging children to imagine they are deep-sea explorers discovering new fish species.", "DevelopmentalGoals": ["Fine Motor Skills", "Creative Expression", "Narrative Thinking", "Social Cooperation"]}	Published Version	8dece4e2-c70e-4d8f-b94a-b07758be517f	2026-11-05 20:39:21.930392+00
2503d5ca-b7cf-4cd5-a230-443c2ac6cee5	e8b51653-8499-4614-9b90-d33bd527d4f1	1	Shirt Color Fish Match Exploration	Children examine the color of their own shirts and explore a collection of pre-defined animal and fish images to find a matching color. They practice identifying and naming colors while engaging in tactile visual matching.	{"AgeMax": 3, "AgeMin": 3, "Create": "A matched pairing display where children arrange their chosen fish pictures next to portraits of themselves wearing their shirts.", "Together": "Children pair up to compare their shirts with their chosen fish images, practicing friendly conversation and peer sharing.", "Challenge": "Find a fish picture that is the exact same color as your shirt and show it to a friend.", "Materials": ["predefined animal and fish images", "color sorting mats", "magnifying glasses"], "Reflection": "What color is your shirt today, and which fish did you find that matches it?", "ChildChoice": "Children independently decide how to search through the fish images and choose which matching fish they want to present.", "Environment": "Indoor", "MagicMoment": "The moment of joyful realization when a child holds up a bright blue fish and excitedly points to their matching blue shirt.", "GroupSizeMax": 4, "GroupSizeMin": 4, "Accomplishment": "Successfully identifying their shirt color and matching it correctly to the corresponding fish picture.", "ExecutionGuide": {"Ask": "How can you tell that this fish matches the color of your shirt?", "Try": "Try finding a fish that is your second favorite color if your first match is hard to find.", "Watch": "Watch for children independently holding fish pictures up against their shirts to check the color match.", "Phases": [{"Name": "Shirt Color Discovery", "ChildrenDo": "Look at their shirts, point to the fabric, and name their shirt colors with teacher support.", "TeacherDoes": "Model naming colors clearly and help children inspect their clothing.", "DurationMinutes": 5}, {"Name": "Fish Matching Hunt", "ChildrenDo": "Search through the fish images to locate one that matches their shirt color.", "TeacherDoes": "Observe children as they compare colors and offer supportive guidance when needed.", "DurationMinutes": 10}, {"Name": "Peer Share and Wrap-Up", "ChildrenDo": "Show their matching fish to a friend and place the images back into the baskets.", "TeacherDoes": "Facilitate gentle sharing between peers and guide clean-up.", "DurationMinutes": 5}], "Safety": ["Ensure laminated image edges are smooth and safe for young hands."], "Closing": "Gather together for a quick wave goodbye to our colorful fish friends.", "Extensions": ["Sort all available fish images into large color category hoops on the floor."], "Adaptations": ["Provide a smaller selection of high-contrast fish images for children who need simplified choices."], "Preparation": ["Print and laminate a diverse set of fish and animal images in distinct solid colors.", "Arrange the image collection on a low accessible table."], "MaterialSetup": ["Place fish images neatly in shallow baskets according to color families."], "EnvironmentSetup": ["Set up a bright table area with plenty of space for children to sit and sort images."], "TeacherIntroduction": "Look down at your shirt today! Can you find a fish in our collection that matches your shirt color?", "LittleMomentOpportunity": "Kneel beside a quieter child to celebrate their color match discovery together.", "SuggestedDurationMinutes": 20}, "TeacherGuidance": "1. Lay out the predefined animal and fish images on a low table. 2. Ask children to look at their shirts and name their colors aloud. 3. Guide children to search the images to find a fish that matches their shirt color. 4. Encourage children to share their match with a peer.", "DevelopmentalGoals": []}	Initial Creation	8dece4e2-c70e-4d8f-b94a-b07758be517f	2026-11-05 21:09:54.421884+00
92c148d2-cee9-488b-a479-d1366e326c54	e8b51653-8499-4614-9b90-d33bd527d4f1	2	The Magical Color Quest	Children become color explorers on a mission to find the 'missing' fish that matches their own vibrant shirt colors, turning a simple matching task into an exciting treasure hunt through a sea of colors.	{"AgeMax": 5, "AgeMin": 3, "Create": "Children create a 'Color Coral Reef' by pinning their matched fish onto a large blue fabric backdrop next to a photo of themselves.", "Together": "Children work as a team of explorers, helping each other spot matching colors and celebrating every successful rescue with a high-five.", "Challenge": "Can you dive into our colorful sea and rescue the fish that matches your shirt?", "Materials": ["Laminated colorful fish cutouts", "Blue fabric or paper backdrop", "Magnifying glasses for 'explorers'", "Clips or tape for the reef display", "Small baskets for the 'sea'"], "Reflection": "If your shirt could turn into a fish, what color would it be and where would it swim in our reef?", "ChildChoice": "Children choose their own path through the 'sea' to find their match and decide where to place their fish in the coral reef display.", "Environment": "Indoor", "MagicMoment": "The giggles that erupt when a child discovers a fish that is the exact same shade as their shirt and 'swims' it over to the reef.", "GroupSizeMax": 6, "GroupSizeMin": 2, "Accomplishment": "Successfully identifying their shirt color and navigating the sea to find a matching friend.", "ExecutionGuide": {"Ask": "What clues did you use to find your fish in the deep blue sea?", "Try": "Try swapping fish with a friend to see if you can find a match for their shirt instead!", "Watch": "Watch for children comparing their shirt fabric directly to the fish images to verify the match.", "Phases": [{"Name": "The Explorer Briefing", "ChildrenDo": "Look at their shirts and practice naming their colors with the Sea Captain.", "TeacherDoes": "Use an enthusiastic, adventurous tone to set the stage for the hunt.", "DurationMinutes": 5}, {"Name": "The Great Fish Rescue", "ChildrenDo": "Search the blue fabric 'sea' to find a fish that matches their shirt color.", "TeacherDoes": "Guide children to look closely and encourage them to compare their shirts to the fish.", "DurationMinutes": 15}, {"Name": "Building the Coral Reef", "ChildrenDo": "Place their rescued fish onto the reef display.", "TeacherDoes": "Help children attach their fish and admire the colorful display together.", "DurationMinutes": 5}], "Safety": ["Ensure all materials are non-toxic and edges are soft.", "Keep the floor area clear of tripping hazards."], "Closing": "Gather around the reef to applaud all the brave explorers for their successful rescue mission.", "Extensions": ["Add patterns to the fish (stripes, spots) to add a layer of complexity to the matching."], "Adaptations": ["Use fewer fish for children who get overwhelmed by too many choices."], "Preparation": ["Create a 'sea' area using blue fabric.", "Hide fish cutouts inside baskets or tucked near the fabric."], "MaterialSetup": ["Scatter the fish images throughout the blue fabric area to look like they are swimming."], "EnvironmentSetup": ["Clear a floor space for the 'sea' and a wall space for the 'reef'."], "TeacherIntroduction": "Ahoy explorers! Our colorful fish have gotten lost in the deep blue sea. Can you look at your shirt and find the fish that matches your color to bring it home to our reef?", "LittleMomentOpportunity": "Quietly join a child who is searching and whisper, 'I see a splash of red over there, could that be your match?'", "SuggestedDurationMinutes": 25}, "TeacherGuidance": "1. Set the scene by acting as a 'Sea Captain' leading the exploration. 2. Encourage children to use their 'explorer eyes' to scan the table. 3. Celebrate each match as a successful rescue mission. 4. Facilitate the creation of the group reef display.", "DevelopmentalGoals": ["Color recognition and naming", "Visual discrimination", "Social collaboration", "Fine motor coordination"]}	Draft Saved	8dece4e2-c70e-4d8f-b94a-b07758be517f	2026-11-05 21:10:09.579473+00
