5b50e169-3ca3-4c38-ba4e-a94f4f8df3bf	ef33ae5e-0972-431c-9af4-0ed1900d8e04	1	Sensory Vegetable Garden Discovery	Children engage in a tactile exploration of vegetables, identifying textures and shapes through touch and sight. This activity connects real-world vegetable characteristics to the images on the display board.	{"AgeMax": 3, "AgeMin": 3, "Create": "A vegetable sorting tray grouped by color and shape.", "Together": "Children work in pairs to compare the items in their hands with the images on the board.", "Challenge": "Find a real vegetable that matches the picture on the board.", "Materials": ["Real vegetables (carrots, broccoli, peppers)", "Vegetable image display board", "Sorting trays"], "Reflection": "Which vegetable was the smoothest to touch?", "ChildChoice": "Children decide which vegetable to pick up and explore first.", "Environment": "Indoor", "MagicMoment": "The look of surprise when a child realizes a real carrot is the same shape as the picture on the wall.", "GroupSizeMax": 4, "GroupSizeMin": 4, "Accomplishment": "Successfully matching three different vegetables to their corresponding images.", "ExecutionGuide": {"Ask": "What does this vegetable feel like in your hand?", "Try": "Sort the vegetables by color instead of name.", "Watch": "Observe how children use their fingers to trace the shapes of the vegetables.", "Phases": [{"Name": "Warm-Up / Introduction", "ChildrenDo": "Gather around the table and look at the real vegetables.", "TeacherDoes": "Introduce each vegetable by name and invite children to touch them.", "DurationMinutes": 5}, {"Name": "Hands-On Exploration", "ChildrenDo": "Pick up a vegetable, name it, and walk to the board to point at the matching image.", "TeacherDoes": "Provide encouragement and help children identify the names if they get stuck.", "DurationMinutes": 15}, {"Name": "Reflection & Clean-Up", "ChildrenDo": "Return the vegetables to the basket and share their favorite one.", "TeacherDoes": "Help children organize the materials back into the storage bins.", "DurationMinutes": 5}], "Safety": ["Ensure all vegetables are clean and safe for handling", "Supervise closely during tactile play"], "Closing": "Gather in a circle to sing a quick song about eating healthy vegetables.", "Extensions": ["Bring in a magnifying glass to look at the texture of the vegetable skin"], "Adaptations": ["Provide larger vegetables for children who need help with fine motor control"], "Preparation": ["Wash all real vegetables thoroughly", "Ensure the display board is at eye level"], "MaterialSetup": ["Sort vegetables into baskets by type"], "EnvironmentSetup": ["Place the display board in a quiet corner", "Arrange the table near the board"], "TeacherIntroduction": "Today we are going to be vegetable detectives and find our favorite veggies on the board!", "LittleMomentOpportunity": "Sit with a child who is shy and help them point to their favorite vegetable on the board.", "SuggestedDurationMinutes": 25}, "TeacherGuidance": "1. Lay out real vegetables on a low table. 2. Encourage children to touch and name them. 3. Guide them to walk to the board to find the match.", "DevelopmentalGoals": []}	Initial Creation	8dece4e2-c70e-4d8f-b94a-b07758be517f	2026-11-05 21:57:38.525515+00
2152fb9e-d787-4fa3-aeee-2a2b3d7f569b	ef33ae5e-0972-431c-9af4-0ed1900d8e04	2	The Vegetable Garden Treasure Hunt	Children become garden explorers on a mission to rescue 'lost' vegetables and return them to their rightful homes on the garden wall. This tactile adventure turns simple identification into a playful quest for discovery.	{"AgeMax": 5, "AgeMin": 3, "Create": "A vibrant 'Garden Map' display where vegetables are sorted by their color and texture.", "Together": "Partners work as a team of garden explorers to navigate the space and match their found treasures to the wall.", "Challenge": "Can you find the hidden vegetable's home on our garden wall?", "Materials": ["Assorted real vegetables (carrots, broccoli, peppers, cucumbers)", "Illustrated garden wall display", "Woven 'treasure' baskets", "Magnifying glasses for 'detective' work"], "Reflection": "Which vegetable felt like a bumpy secret, and which one felt as smooth as a stone?", "ChildChoice": "Children choose which 'treasure' to hunt for first from the mystery garden basket.", "Environment": "Indoor", "MagicMoment": "The excitement when a child successfully 'plants' their vegetable by matching it to the correct picture on the wall.", "GroupSizeMax": 6, "GroupSizeMin": 2, "Accomplishment": "Successfully reuniting all the vegetables with their pictures on the garden wall.", "ExecutionGuide": {"Ask": "If this vegetable could talk, what kind of garden story would it tell us?", "Try": "Invite children to sort the vegetables by their texture (bumpy vs. smooth) rather than just by type.", "Watch": "Observe how children use their hands to explore the unique bumps, stems, and skins of the vegetables.", "Phases": [{"Name": "The Garden Hunt", "ChildrenDo": "Search the room for hidden vegetables and use magnifying glasses to inspect their textures.", "TeacherDoes": "Narrate the adventure and encourage children to describe what they find using sensory words.", "DurationMinutes": 10}, {"Name": "The Homecoming", "ChildrenDo": "Carry their vegetable treasure to the garden wall and match it to the correct picture.", "TeacherDoes": "Provide prompts to help children compare the real vegetable to the illustration.", "DurationMinutes": 10}, {"Name": "Garden Celebration", "ChildrenDo": "Gather in a circle to share which vegetable was the most fun to find.", "TeacherDoes": "Lead a simple 'Garden Song' to celebrate the successful rescue.", "DurationMinutes": 5}], "Safety": ["Ensure all vegetables are clean and safe for handling", "Supervise movement to ensure children walk carefully while carrying their treasures"], "Closing": "Celebrate the garden's return to order with a group high-five for our hard-working detectives.", "Extensions": ["Create vegetable prints using non-toxic paint to make a 'Garden Mural'"], "Adaptations": ["Use larger, more distinct vegetables for children who need extra support with identification"], "Preparation": ["Wash all vegetables thoroughly", "Create an inviting garden wall display at child height"], "MaterialSetup": ["Hide vegetables in baskets around the room to turn it into a hunt"], "EnvironmentSetup": ["Create a 'garden' corner with baskets", "Place the garden wall display on the opposite side of the room to encourage movement"], "TeacherIntroduction": "Oh no! The vegetables have wandered away from the garden! Are you ready to be garden detectives and help them find their way back home?", "LittleMomentOpportunity": "Take a quiet moment to let a child look through the magnifying glass at a vegetable's tiny details.", "SuggestedDurationMinutes": 25}, "TeacherGuidance": "1. Set the scene with a story about a garden that lost its vegetables. 2. Encourage children to use their senses to describe their findings. 3. Celebrate each match as a successful homecoming.", "DevelopmentalGoals": ["Sensory processing and tactile discrimination", "Visual matching and categorization", "Collaborative social play", "Vocabulary development"]}	Draft Saved	8dece4e2-c70e-4d8f-b94a-b07758be517f	2026-11-05 21:58:15.687879+00
