f0fa25a2-84a1-4eed-bd40-1d8d260bdc64	10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001	The Great Wobble-O-Saurus & the Wacky, Shakey Towers!	A super playful, giggle-filled building adventure where children work together to build the silliest, most gravity-defying towers for their toy animal buddies, while dodging the friendly 'Wobble-O-Saurus' earthquake!	Published	{"AgeMax": 3, "AgeMin": 2, "Create": "Stacking foam cups, cardboard tubes, and blocks onto a wobbly cushion or tray, and adding funny decorations like googly eyes to make a silly home for their toy animals.", "Together": "A team of giggling builders passing cups with funny sound effects, stacking silly objects, and gasping together as their tower does a wiggly dance!", "Challenge": "Work with a buddy to build a wacky, super-tall tower on a shaky foundation that can survive the silly 'Wobble-O-Saurus' shake!", "Materials": ["Foam cups", "Cardboard tubes", "Soft sponges or cushions (to use as shaky foundations)", "Small plastic toy animals", "Googly eyes on tape", "Feather duster or pool noodle (for the Wobble-O-Saurus)"], "Reflection": "Pretending to be wobbly towers themselves, shaking from side to side, and then collapsing onto the floor in a silly slow-motion melt together!", "ChildChoice": "Choosing their toy animal partner, naming their tower a silly name (like 'Captain Cup-Cake'), and deciding if their building gets a cup-hat, a slide, or a secret trampoline!", "Environment": "Indoor", "MagicMoment": "The hilarious suspense as the teacher pretends to be the 'Wobble-O-Saurus', making funny rumbling noises, while the children quickly strike a funny 'freeze pose' to protect their shaky masterpiece!", "GroupSizeMax": 10, "GroupSizeMin": 4, "Accomplishment": "Doing the 'Wobbly-Wobble Dance of Victory' with your partner when your tower stands tall—or collapses in a glorious cloud of giggles!", "ExecutionGuide": {"Ask": "What silly sound does your tower make when it wiggles? Can you show me your best Wobble-O-Saurus face?", "Try": "Try adding a giant foam cup hat to the very top of your tower to see if it makes it wobble even more!", "Watch": "Look for children who laugh when things fall, and encourage teammates who help each other rebuild with even sillier, wider designs.", "Phases": [{"Name": "Partner Up & Pick a Buddy", "ChildrenDo": "Choose a partner and select a toy animal who needs a 'wacky tower house'. Give the animal a funny voice.", "TeacherDoes": "Help children form pairs and pass out the animal toys with silly sound effects.", "DurationMinutes": 3}, {"Name": "Build the Wiggle-Tower", "ChildrenDo": "Stack cups and tubes on top of the wobbly sponge foundation, making funny 'beep-boop' sounds for every block added.", "TeacherDoes": "Circulate, admire the wacky designs, and suggest adding silly details like 'cup-hats' or googly-eye windows.", "DurationMinutes": 10}, {"Name": "The Wobble-O-Saurus Shake!", "ChildrenDo": "Hold hands or strike a funny 'shield pose' over their tower as the teacher gently taps their wobbly sponge foundation.", "TeacherDoes": "Pretend to be the Wobble-O-Saurus! Make gentle rumbling sounds, gently tap the sponges to make the towers wiggle, and cheer wildly when they tumble.", "DurationMinutes": 5}, {"Name": "Wobble Dance Celebration", "ChildrenDo": "Celebrate their towers (standing or fallen!) by doing a silly, shaky wiggle dance with their partners.", "TeacherDoes": "Lead a high-energy 'Wobble Dance' and help children transition to clean-up.", "DurationMinutes": 2}], "Safety": ["Ensure toy animals are large enough to not be choking hazards.", "Keep building materials lightweight (foam cups, cardboard) so falling structures are completely safe and quiet."], "Closing": "High-five your partner, give your toy animal a cozy squeeze, and let's do one last giant shake-out wobble!", "Extensions": ["Use a flashlight to cast giant 'wobbly monster shadows' of the towers on the classroom wall!", "Add colorful socks to slide over the cardboard tubes to give the towers silly, bright patterns."], "Adaptations": ["For children who get frustrated when towers fall, build directly on the solid floor instead of a sponge foundation to make it sturdy.", "For a quieter experience, use soft dish sponges as the building blocks to make a completely silent, sneaky tower."], "Preparation": ["Gather foam cups, cardboard tubes, and sponges.", "Set up building stations on the rug with plenty of space between pairs."], "MaterialSetup": ["Place a soft sponge or cushion at each station as the 'Wobble Zone' foundation.", "Put baskets of foam cups, tubes, and toy animals within easy reach of each station."], "EnvironmentSetup": ["Clear a wide floor space so children can easily sit in pairs and have room for falling cups to scatter safely."], "TeacherIntroduction": "Oh no! The friendly Wobble-O-Saurus is coming to town, and they love to dance! Can you and your partner build a wacky, super-tall tower for your toy animals that can survive the Great Wobble Dance? Let's build!", "LittleMomentOpportunity": "When a tower inevitably falls, gasp dramatically, fall to the floor in a silly slow-motion melt, and shout 'Boom-shaka-laka!' to turn a collapse into the absolute highlight of the game.", "SuggestedDurationMinutes": 20}, "TeacherGuidance": "Embody the playful Wobble-O-Saurus! Walk around making silly, low rumbling noises, warning children of 'gentle tremors' coming. Use a soft feather duster to gently tickle or blow a 'silly breeze' on their towers. Keep the energy light, dramatic, and focused on the joy of rebuilding together rather than keeping things perfect."}	df5d8828-f7cb-4250-9cd1-dba1d787d531	2026-10-05 02:56:57.971218+00	2026-10-07 22:56:14.698535+00	20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
a7409952-18ab-47e0-a7ab-a5b53426343f	10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001	The Wiggle-Wobble Clay Monster Party (Focus: Make It More Playful)	Children wake up sleeping lumps of clay with silly tickles and splats, then transform them into goofy, wiggly monster friends using shaky googly eyes, wiggly pipe cleaners, and fluffy tickle-feathers. Adapted with emphasis on: Make it more playful.	Published	{"AgeMax": 3, "AgeMin": 2, "Create": "Pinch a goofy nose, press in tons of googly eyes, add bouncy zig-zag pipe cleaner legs, and give your monster a fluffy feather tail for tickling.", "Together": "Let's pat, squeeze, and gently splat our clay on the table! We'll tickle the clay to 'wake it up' and make funny yawning noises together.", "Challenge": "Can you make a super silly, wiggly clay monster that loves to dance and make funny noises? Challenge adaptation: Make it more playful.", "Materials": ["Brightly colored playdough or air-dry clay", "Assorted sizes of googly eyes", "Colorful pipe cleaners (some pre-bent into zig-zags)", "Fluffy craft feathers", "Soft mini pom-poms for silly noses", "Small plastic cups (to hide the craft parts under)"], "Reflection": "Show me your monster's favorite dance move! What silly sound does it make when you tickle its nose?", "ChildChoice": "Deciding how many eyes to stack, bending pipe cleaners into wild shapes, and inventing their monster's signature silly voice and dance move.", "Environment": "Indoor / Outdoor", "MagicMoment": "When a child tickles their finished monster's tummy with a feather and lets out a huge, shared giggle as they act out the monster's funny voice.", "GroupSizeMax": 10, "GroupSizeMin": 4, "Accomplishment": "Hosting a wild 'Monster Dance Party' on the table, making all our creations wiggle, shake, and shout silly words together.", "ExecutionGuide": {"Ask": "What is your monster's name? Does it make a squeaky sound or a roaring sound when it wiggles?", "Try": "If a monster's wiggly leg falls off, make a dramatic 'Oh no!' sound, poke a deep finger hole into the clay together, and pinch it tight while saying '1, 2, 3, stick!'", "Watch": "Watch for children giggling and engaging in pretend play. Keep an eye out to make sure small googly eyes and pom-poms stay on the trays and out of mouths.", "Phases": [{"Name": "Wake Up & Splat!", "ChildrenDo": "Tickle, squeeze, and gently splat their clay on the tray to warm it up, making silly 'wake up' sounds.", "TeacherDoes": "Lead the stretching and squeezing with funny sound effects like 'streeeetch' and 'splat!'.", "DurationMinutes": 6}, {"Name": "The Magic Reveal", "ChildrenDo": "Lift up their surprise cups to discover the eyes, wiggly pipe cleaners, and feathers hidden underneath.", "TeacherDoes": "Gasp in excitement and encourage children to name the colorful treasures they found under their 'surprise hats'.", "DurationMinutes": 4}, {"Name": "Build a Goofy Friend", "ChildrenDo": "Press eyes, zig-zag legs, and feathers into their clay to build a silly monster face and body.", "TeacherDoes": "Circulate and make funny 'boop' and 'pop' noises as kids press items into the clay.", "DurationMinutes": 10}, {"Name": "The Monster Dance Party!", "ChildrenDo": "Bounce their finished monsters on the table dance floor, making them wiggle and make silly noises.", "TeacherDoes": "Play some upbeat, playful background music and narrate the funny dance moves the monsters are doing.", "DurationMinutes": 5}], "Safety": ["Ensure pipe cleaner ends are tucked or folded so they are not sharp.", "Actively supervise to prevent any mouthing of the small googly eyes or pom-poms."], "Closing": "Let's tuck our tired monsters into their trays for a nap. Let's whisper, 'Goodnight, silly monsters, thank you for dancing with us!'", "Extensions": ["Create a simple 'Monster Freeze Dance' game where children freeze their clay monsters when the music stops.", "Provide cardboard boxes as 'monster cars' to slide them around the room."], "Adaptations": ["For younger toddlers: Focus purely on poking big craft sticks and giant eyes into the clay to make 'peek-a-boo' faces.", "For older children: Challenge them to make a monster that can balance on one giant wiggly leg."], "Preparation": ["Roll the clay into round 'sleeping' balls.", "Bend several pipe cleaners into zig-zags and spirals.", "Hide the eyes, feathers, and pom-poms under plastic cups on each tray like secret surprise hats."], "MaterialSetup": ["Place a 'sleeping' ball of clay on each tray.", "Place the upside-down surprise cups next to the clay."], "EnvironmentSetup": ["Create a 'Monster Dance Floor' by taping a bright sheet of paper in the center of the table.", "Set up individual trays for each child to contain the playdough splats."], "TeacherIntroduction": "Shh... look! Our clay balls are fast asleep! On the count of three, let's give them a gentle tickle and shout 'WAKE UP, CLAY!' One, two, three... WAKE UP!", "LittleMomentOpportunity": "When a child puts an eye in a weird place like the bottom of the clay, dramatically pretend the monster is looking at your toes and giggle together about its 'toe-vision'.", "SuggestedDurationMinutes": 25}, "TeacherGuidance": "Keep the energy high and full of pretend play. Use your voice to bring the clay to life—giggle when you touch it, make 'boop' sounds when adding eyes, and encourage children to talk to their monsters. Focus on the joy of creation rather than making a perfect figure.", "DevelopmentalGoals": []}	df5d8828-f7cb-4250-9cd1-dba1d787d531	2026-10-07 22:42:59.844585+00	2026-10-15 00:19:44.111307+00	20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
3a48a470-63cd-492c-ba6f-8dd3032205cf	10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001	The Wobbly, Bubbly Scribble-Ship Circus!	A highly interactive, laughter-packed water adventure where children transform paper into bouncy circus boats with colorful crayon armor, choose a silly squeaky animal buddy, and blow a towering mountain of blue giggling bubbles to build a protective shield against the ticklish Bubble Monster!	Published	{"AgeMax": 4, "AgeMin": 3, "Create": "Decorate your paper boat with a super-thick layer of colorful crayon wax, pop your silly animal buddy inside, and blow a wild storm of bubbles to guide your ship to a safe, squishy sponge island!", "Together": "We will do the 'seaweed-wiggle' dance, wear our paper boats as goofy hats, scribble at lightning-fast speed, and blow a colossal, wobbly mountain of blue bubbles!", "Challenge": "Can you give your wobbly paper boat a shiny coat of magic crayon armor to keep your ticklish squeaky-animal passenger safe from the giant giggle-bubble storm?", "Materials": ["Square colorful paper (15cm x 15cm)", "Chunky wax crayons", "Shallow plastic trays", "Soapy water with blue food coloring", "Small squeaky toy animals", "Colorful kitchen sponges cut into fun shapes", "Drinking straws"], "Reflection": "What funny sound did your animal friend make when the bubbles tickled their toes? What was your boat's favorite dance move today?", "ChildChoice": "Children choose their own squeaky animal passenger, pick their favorite neon crayon colors, decide on a goofy name for their ship, and choose which shaped sponge island to park on.", "Environment": "Indoor / Outdoor", "MagicMoment": "The explosive laughter when the blue bubbles grow so tall they spill over the tray and land on the children's noses, giving them instant 'bubble mustaches'!", "GroupSizeMax": 10, "GroupSizeMin": 4, "Accomplishment": "Successfully rescuing their animal buddy from the tickle-storm and giving their partner a high-five using a squishy, wet sponge!", "ExecutionGuide": {"Ask": "What silly sound does your animal buddy make when a bubble tickles their tummy, and what is the name of your boat's favorite dance move?", "Try": "Try holding your crayon like a magic wand and scribble-scribbling as fast as a zooming rocket to make your boat's shiny wax armor super-strong!", "Watch": "Watch for silly sailors who might try to sip the soapy bubble juice through their straws; playfully show them how to blow 'birthday candle' winds OUT, and keep an eye out for ultra-soggy paper bottoms that need extra crayon scribbles!", "Phases": [{"Name": "The Scribble-Race Frenzy", "ChildrenDo": "Scribble-color the bottom of their paper boat as fast as they can with wax crayons to make it waterproof.", "TeacherDoes": "Plays fast, goofy circus music and calls out silly coloring styles: 'Color like a hyper monkey! Color like a slow-motion sloth!'", "DurationMinutes": 7}, {"Name": "The Bubble-Pop Circus", "ChildrenDo": "Place their squeaky toy in their boat, set it in the water tray, and blow through their straws to create a giant, foaming mountain of blue bubbles to float their boat to the sponge island.", "TeacherDoes": "Leads a dramatic 'bubble-blowing countdown' and cheers loudly as the bubbles grow, pointing out who has the tallest bubble mountain or the best bubble mustache.", "DurationMinutes": 13}, {"Name": "Silly Captain Parade", "ChildrenDo": "Fold their paper into a simple boat shape, place it on their heads like a funny hat, and march in place making goofy engine noises.", "TeacherDoes": "Guides the folding using silly names for the folds ('hot dog fold', 'bouncy triangle fold') and snaps imaginary silly photos of the children's hat styles.", "DurationMinutes": 5}], "Safety": ["Remind children continuously to only blow OUT, never suck IN through the straws.", "Keep plenty of dry towels handy to mop up any slippery soapy splashes on the floor immediately."], "Closing": "Lead all captains in parking their boats, giving their squeaky toys a warm towel-blanket tuck-in, and doing a giant group 'Wobbly Seaweed Dance' to celebrate their success!", "Extensions": ["Have a 'Bubble Nose-Pop' game where kids try to pop the tallest bubble using only the tip of their nose without touching it with their hands!", "Add a drop of red paint to the sponge islands to watch the blue bubble water magically swirl into purple when they arrive!"], "Adaptations": ["For younger children, pre-fold the boats so they can jump straight into the coloring and bubble-blowing play.", "For older kids, challenge them to build a 'bubble bridge' across the tray using two straws at the same time."], "Preparation": ["Mix water, blue food coloring, and plenty of dish soap in the plastic trays.", "Cut colorful sponges into star, cloud, or heart shapes to act as 'Silly Sponge Islands' and place them inside the trays."], "MaterialSetup": ["Place crayons in bright baskets, stack the square paper, and cover the water trays with colorful towels to make the 'Big Bubble Reveal' exciting."], "EnvironmentSetup": ["Create a 'Silly Shipyard' coloring table with bright decorations and a nearby 'Bubbly Ocean Arena' for the water play trays."], "TeacherIntroduction": "Welcome to the Bubbly Scribble-Ship Circus! I am your Ringleader! A giant, ticklish Bubble Monster is tickling our toes! We need to make shiny, crayon-armored circus boats, grab our squeakiest animal friends, and blow a huge, wobbly shield of blue bubbles to protect them! Who is ready to get silly?", "LittleMomentOpportunity": "The pure joy when a child successfully blows a bubble dome so big that it completely encapsulates their little toy animal passenger, leading to gasps and giggles.", "SuggestedDurationMinutes": 25}, "TeacherGuidance": "Become a cartoon character! Wear a silly hat, use funny sound effects (whoosh, pop, boing), make giant cartoonish facial expressions, and treat every step like an exciting, playful game.", "DevelopmentalGoals": []}	df5d8828-f7cb-4250-9cd1-dba1d787d531	2026-10-08 02:24:08.30363+00	2026-10-09 13:54:21.441684+00	20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
28c7e99a-7613-4d5d-ba9f-f0b92428d5c8	10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001	The Wiggle-Wobble Clay Monster Party (Focus: Make It More Playful)	Children wake up sleeping lumps of clay with silly tickles and splats, then transform them into goofy, wiggly monster friends using shaky googly eyes, wiggly pipe cleaners, and fluffy tickle-feathers. Adapted with emphasis on: Make it more playful.	Approved	{"AgeMax": 3, "AgeMin": 2, "Create": "Pinch a goofy nose, press in tons of googly eyes, add bouncy zig-zag pipe cleaner legs, and give your monster a fluffy feather tail for tickling.", "Together": "Let's pat, squeeze, and gently splat our clay on the table! We'll tickle the clay to 'wake it up' and make funny yawning noises together.", "Challenge": "Can you make a super silly, wiggly clay monster that loves to dance and make funny noises? Challenge adaptation: Make it more playful.", "Materials": ["Brightly colored playdough or air-dry clay", "Assorted sizes of googly eyes", "Colorful pipe cleaners (some pre-bent into zig-zags)", "Fluffy craft feathers", "Soft mini pom-poms for silly noses", "Small plastic cups (to hide the craft parts under)"], "Reflection": "Show me your monster's favorite dance move! What silly sound does it make when you tickle its nose?", "Environment": "Indoor / Outdoor", "MagicMoment": "When a child tickles their finished monster's tummy with a feather and lets out a huge, shared giggle as they act out the monster's funny voice.", "GroupSizeMax": 10, "GroupSizeMin": 4, "Accomplishment": "Hosting a wild 'Monster Dance Party' on the table, making all our creations wiggle, shake, and shout silly words together.", "ExecutionGuide": {"Ask": "What is your monster's name? Does it make a squeaky sound or a roaring sound when it wiggles?", "Try": "If a monster's wiggly leg falls off, make a dramatic 'Oh no!' sound, poke a deep finger hole into the clay together, and pinch it tight while saying '1, 2, 3, stick!'", "Watch": "Watch for children giggling and engaging in pretend play. Keep an eye out to make sure small googly eyes and pom-poms stay on the trays and out of mouths.", "Phases": [{"Name": "Wake Up & Splat!", "ChildrenDo": "Tickle, squeeze, and gently splat their clay on the tray to warm it up, making silly 'wake up' sounds.", "TeacherDoes": "Lead the stretching and squeezing with funny sound effects like 'streeeetch' and 'splat!'.", "DurationMinutes": 6}, {"Name": "The Magic Reveal", "ChildrenDo": "Lift up their surprise cups to discover the eyes, wiggly pipe cleaners, and feathers hidden underneath.", "TeacherDoes": "Gasp in excitement and encourage children to name the colorful treasures they found under their 'surprise hats'.", "DurationMinutes": 4}, {"Name": "Build a Goofy Friend", "ChildrenDo": "Press eyes, zig-zag legs, and feathers into their clay to build a silly monster face and body.", "TeacherDoes": "Circulate and make funny 'boop' and 'pop' noises as kids press items into the clay.", "DurationMinutes": 10}, {"Name": "The Monster Dance Party!", "ChildrenDo": "Bounce their finished monsters on the table dance floor, making them wiggle and make silly noises.", "TeacherDoes": "Play some upbeat, playful background music and narrate the funny dance moves the monsters are doing.", "DurationMinutes": 5}], "Safety": ["Ensure pipe cleaner ends are tucked or folded so they are not sharp.", "Actively supervise to prevent any mouthing of the small googly eyes or pom-poms."], "Closing": "Let's tuck our tired monsters into their trays for a nap. Let's whisper, 'Goodnight, silly monsters, thank you for dancing with us!'", "Extensions": ["Create a simple 'Monster Freeze Dance' game where children freeze their clay monsters when the music stops.", "Provide cardboard boxes as 'monster cars' to slide them around the room."], "Adaptations": ["For younger toddlers: Focus purely on poking big craft sticks and giant eyes into the clay to make 'peek-a-boo' faces.", "For older children: Challenge them to make a monster that can balance on one giant wiggly leg."], "Preparation": ["Roll the clay into round 'sleeping' balls.", "Bend several pipe cleaners into zig-zags and spirals.", "Hide the eyes, feathers, and pom-poms under plastic cups on each tray like secret surprise hats."], "MaterialSetup": ["Place a 'sleeping' ball of clay on each tray.", "Place the upside-down surprise cups next to the clay."], "EnvironmentSetup": ["Create a 'Monster Dance Floor' by taping a bright sheet of paper in the center of the table.", "Set up individual trays for each child to contain the playdough splats."], "TeacherIntroduction": "Shh... look! Our clay balls are fast asleep! On the count of three, let's give them a gentle tickle and shout 'WAKE UP, CLAY!' One, two, three... WAKE UP!", "LittleMomentOpportunity": "When a child puts an eye in a weird place like the bottom of the clay, dramatically pretend the monster is looking at your toes and giggle together about its 'toe-vision'.", "SuggestedDurationMinutes": 25}, "TeacherGuidance": "Keep the energy high and full of pretend play. Use your voice to bring the clay to life—giggle when you touch it, make 'boop' sounds when adding eyes, and encourage children to talk to their monsters. Focus on the joy of creation rather than making a perfect figure.", "DevelopmentalGoals": [], "_platformProvenance": {"Version": 1, "ImportedAt": "2026-10-15T22:06:46.4829443+00:00", "PlatformExperienceId": "b1395d93-9d90-4e64-9226-a1c201b651ce"}}	50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002	2026-10-15 22:06:46.490997+00	2026-10-15 22:06:46.490998+00	ee79a62a-90be-476a-a22a-cd4d8a2eaac2
