ef33ae5e-0972-431c-9af4-0ed1900d8e04	8a3f0f3e-9c84-4dfa-8342-f8546aedfa52	The Vegetable Garden Treasure Hunt	Children become garden explorers on a mission to rescue 'lost' vegetables and return them to their rightful homes on the garden wall. This tactile adventure turns simple identification into a playful quest for discovery.	Published	{"AgeMax": 5, "AgeMin": 3, "Create": "A vibrant 'Garden Map' display where vegetables are sorted by their color and texture.", "Together": "Partners work as a team of garden explorers to navigate the space and match their found treasures to the wall.", "Challenge": "Can you find the hidden vegetable's home on our garden wall?", "Materials": ["Assorted real vegetables (carrots, broccoli, peppers, cucumbers)", "Illustrated garden wall display", "Woven 'treasure' baskets", "Magnifying glasses for 'detective' work"], "Reflection": "Which vegetable felt like a bumpy secret, and which one felt as smooth as a stone?", "ChildChoice": "Children choose which 'treasure' to hunt for first from the mystery garden basket.", "Environment": "Indoor", "MagicMoment": "The excitement when a child successfully 'plants' their vegetable by matching it to the correct picture on the wall.", "GroupSizeMax": 6, "GroupSizeMin": 2, "Accomplishment": "Successfully reuniting all the vegetables with their pictures on the garden wall.", "ExecutionGuide": {"Ask": "If this vegetable could talk, what kind of garden story would it tell us?", "Try": "Invite children to sort the vegetables by their texture (bumpy vs. smooth) rather than just by type.", "Watch": "Observe how children use their hands to explore the unique bumps, stems, and skins of the vegetables.", "Phases": [{"Name": "The Garden Hunt", "ChildrenDo": "Search the room for hidden vegetables and use magnifying glasses to inspect their textures.", "TeacherDoes": "Narrate the adventure and encourage children to describe what they find using sensory words.", "DurationMinutes": 10}, {"Name": "The Homecoming", "ChildrenDo": "Carry their vegetable treasure to the garden wall and match it to the correct picture.", "TeacherDoes": "Provide prompts to help children compare the real vegetable to the illustration.", "DurationMinutes": 10}, {"Name": "Garden Celebration", "ChildrenDo": "Gather in a circle to share which vegetable was the most fun to find.", "TeacherDoes": "Lead a simple 'Garden Song' to celebrate the successful rescue.", "DurationMinutes": 5}], "Safety": ["Ensure all vegetables are clean and safe for handling", "Supervise movement to ensure children walk carefully while carrying their treasures"], "Closing": "Celebrate the garden's return to order with a group high-five for our hard-working detectives.", "Extensions": ["Create vegetable prints using non-toxic paint to make a 'Garden Mural'"], "Adaptations": ["Use larger, more distinct vegetables for children who need extra support with identification"], "Preparation": ["Wash all vegetables thoroughly", "Create an inviting garden wall display at child height"], "MaterialSetup": ["Hide vegetables in baskets around the room to turn it into a hunt"], "EnvironmentSetup": ["Create a 'garden' corner with baskets", "Place the garden wall display on the opposite side of the room to encourage movement"], "TeacherIntroduction": "Oh no! The vegetables have wandered away from the garden! Are you ready to be garden detectives and help them find their way back home?", "LittleMomentOpportunity": "Take a quiet moment to let a child look through the magnifying glass at a vegetable's tiny details.", "SuggestedDurationMinutes": 25}, "TeacherGuidance": "1. Set the scene with a story about a garden that lost its vegetables. 2. Encourage children to use their senses to describe their findings. 3. Celebrate each match as a successful homecoming.", "DevelopmentalGoals": ["Sensory processing and tactile discrimination", "Visual matching and categorization", "Collaborative social play", "Vocabulary development"]}	8dece4e2-c70e-4d8f-b94a-b07758be517f	2026-11-05 21:57:38.525515+00	2026-11-05 21:58:25.416335+00	8a3f0f3e-9c84-4dfa-8342-f8546aedfa52
3dc75d06-88ff-4514-ae90-015d8d0d3a16	8a3f0f3e-9c84-4dfa-8342-f8546aedfa52	The Rainbow Rescue Mission	Oh no! The colorful balls have escaped their rainbow homes and are scattered everywhere. Children become brave color explorers, racing to rescue the balls and return them to their cozy, matching baskets before the rainbow disappears.	Published	{"AgeMax": 5, "AgeMin": 3, "Create": "A vibrant, completed rainbow of sorted balls ready for a celebration.", "Together": "Children work as a team of rescuers, cheering each other on as they hunt for colors and fill the baskets together.", "Challenge": "Can you help every ball find its way back to its matching rainbow home?", "Materials": ["Colorful plastic balls", "Colored baskets or bins", "Fun music for the rescue mission"], "Reflection": "Which color was the fastest to find, and which one was hiding the best?", "ChildChoice": "Children choose which color home to rescue first and decide if they want to hop, skip, or crawl to deliver the balls.", "Environment": "Indoor", "MagicMoment": "The cheer that erupts when the final ball is placed into its home, completing the full rainbow.", "GroupSizeMax": 6, "GroupSizeMin": 2, "Accomplishment": "Successfully reuniting all the colors with their homes through teamwork and fast-paced play.", "ExecutionGuide": {"Ask": "If we found a new color that doesn't have a home, what should we do to help it?", "Try": "Add a 'delivery' challenge where children must balance the ball on a spoon while walking to the basket.", "Watch": "Observe how children navigate the space and how they communicate with peers during the rescue.", "Phases": [{"Name": "The Rescue Mission Begins", "ChildrenDo": "Listen to the mission story and identify the colors of the empty homes.", "TeacherDoes": "Sets the stage with an enthusiastic story and plays upbeat music.", "DurationMinutes": 5}, {"Name": "Color Dash", "ChildrenDo": "Run, hop, or crawl to find balls and return them to the matching colored basket.", "TeacherDoes": "Calls out color clues and encourages children to move in different ways.", "DurationMinutes": 10}, {"Name": "Rainbow Celebration", "ChildrenDo": "Gather around the full baskets to count the colors and celebrate the successful rescue.", "TeacherDoes": "Leads a celebratory dance or song to conclude the mission.", "DurationMinutes": 5}], "Safety": ["Ensure the floor is clear of obstacles", "Encourage walking or hopping rather than running to prevent collisions"], "Closing": "Gather in a circle to share one thing they liked about being a color hero.", "Extensions": ["Create a 'color hunt' map where children must find specific colors in a specific order"], "Adaptations": ["Use fewer colors for younger children", "Provide a 'rescue vehicle' like a small bin to carry multiple balls at once"], "Preparation": ["Scatter the balls across the floor to create a 'lost' scene", "Place the colored baskets in a circle around the room"], "MaterialSetup": ["Ensure baskets are clearly visible and spaced out to encourage movement"], "EnvironmentSetup": ["Clear a large floor area for active movement"], "TeacherIntroduction": "Calling all color explorers! Our rainbow friends are lost and need your help to get back home. Are you ready to go on a rescue mission?", "LittleMomentOpportunity": "Notice a child who is carefully matching a ball and offer a special 'rescue badge' sticker for their great work.", "SuggestedDurationMinutes": 20}, "TeacherGuidance": "1. Set the scene by telling a story about the lost colors. 2. Encourage movement by asking children to 'deliver' the balls in different ways. 3. Celebrate each successful rescue with a high-five or a happy dance.", "DevelopmentalGoals": ["Color recognition", "Categorization skills", "Gross motor movement", "Cooperative play"]}	8dece4e2-c70e-4d8f-b94a-b07758be517f	2026-11-05 23:03:39.840662+00	2026-11-05 23:04:10.190851+00	8a3f0f3e-9c84-4dfa-8342-f8546aedfa52
