,"Watch":"Watch for children giggling and engaging in pretend play. Keep an eye out to make sure small googly eyes and pom-poms stay on the trays and out of mouths.","Phases":[{"Name":"Wake Up \\u0026 Splat!","ChildrenDo":"Tickle, squeeze, and gently splat their clay on the tray to warm it up, making silly \\u0027wake up\\u0027 sounds.","TeacherDoes":"Lead the stretching and squeezing with funny sound effects like \\u0027streeeetch\\u0027 and \\u0027splat!\\u0027.","DurationMinutes":6},{"Name":"The Magic Reveal","ChildrenDo":"Lift up their surprise cups to discover the eyes, wiggly pipe cleaners, and feathers hidden underneath.","TeacherDoes":"Gasp in excitement and encourage children to name the colorful treasures they found under their \\u0027surprise hats\\u0027.","DurationMinutes":4},{"Name":"Build a Goofy Friend","ChildrenDo":"Press eyes, zig-zag legs, and feathers into their clay to build a silly monster face and body.","TeacherDoes":"Circulate and make funny \\u0027boop\\u0027 and \\u0027pop\\u0027 noises as kids press items into the clay.","DurationMinutes":10},{"Name":"The Monster Dance Party!","ChildrenDo":"Bounce their finished monsters on the table dance floor, making them wiggle and make silly noises.","TeacherDoes":"Play some upbeat, playful background music and narrate the funny dance moves the monsters are doing.","DurationMinutes":5}],"Safety":["Ensure pipe cleaner ends are tucked or folded so they are not sharp.","Actively supervise to prevent any mouthing of the small googly eyes or pom-poms."],"Closing":"Let\\u0027s tuck our tired monsters into their trays for a nap. Let\\u0027s whisper, \\u0027Goodnight, silly monsters, thank you for dancing with us!\\u0027","Extensions":["Create a simple \\u0027Monster Freeze Dance\\u0027 game where children freeze their clay monsters when the music stops.","Provide cardboard boxes as \\u0027monster cars\\u0027 to slide them around the room."],"Adaptations":["For younger toddlers: Focus purely on poking big craft sticks and giant eyes into the clay to make \\u0027peek-a-boo\\u0027 faces.","For older children: Challenge them to make a monster that can balance on one giant wiggly leg."],"Preparation":["Roll the clay into round \\u0027sleeping\\u0027 balls.","Bend several pipe cleaners into zig-zags and spirals.","Hide the eyes, feathers, and pom-poms under plastic cups on each tray like secret surprise hats."],"MaterialSetup":["Place a \\u0027sleeping\\u0027 ball of clay on each tray.","Place the upside-down surprise cups next to the clay."],"EnvironmentSetup":["Create a \\u0027Monster Dance Floor\\u0027 by taping a bright sheet of paper in the center of the table.","Set up individual trays for each child to contain the playdough splats."],"TeacherIntroduction":"Shh... look! Our clay balls are fast asleep! On the count of three, let\\u0027s give them a gentle tickle and shout \\u0027WAKE UP, CLAY!\\u0027 One, two, three... WAKE UP!","LittleMomentOpportunity":"When a child puts an eye in a weird place like the bottom of the clay, dramatically pretend the monster is looking at your toes and giggle together about its \\u0027toe-vision\\u0027.","SuggestedDurationMinutes":25},"TeacherGuidance":"Keep the energy high and full of pretend play. Use your voice to bring the clay to life\\u2014giggle when you touch it, make \\u0027boop\\u0027 sounds when adding eyes, and encourage children to talk to their monsters. Focus on the joy of creation rather than making a perfect figure.","DevelopmentalGoals":[]}	Free	0.00	INR	Published	CuratedLicensed	1	4d88e9d7-60d6-4bc2-9e88-5babf43fdc8f	eea60dd8-7d83-44e2-be6c-bff4e67acdb0	a7409952-18ab-47e0-a7ab-a5b53426343f	20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001	\N	2026-10-15 21:59:38.120346+00	2026-10-15 22:05:55.208681+00
1c418ac7-4c75-4353-849c-6751981b646d	The Wobbly, Bubbly Scribble-Ship Circus!	A highly interactive, laughter-packed water adventure where children transform paper into bouncy circus boats with colorful crayon armor, choose a silly squeaky animal buddy, and blow a towering mountain of blue giggling bubbles to build a protective shield against the ticklish Bubble Monster!	Early Childhood	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	{"AgeMax":4,"AgeMin":3,"Create":"Decorate your paper boat with a super-thick layer of colorful crayon wax, pop your silly animal buddy inside, and blow a wild storm of bubbles to guide your ship to a safe, squishy sponge island!","Together":"We will do the \\u0027seaweed-wiggle\\u0027 dance, wear our paper boats as goofy hats, scribble at lightning-fast speed, and blow a colossal, wobbly mountain of blue bubbles!","Challenge":"Can you give your wobbly paper boat a shiny coat of magic crayon armor to keep your ticklish squeaky-animal passenger safe from the giant giggle-bubble storm?","Materials":["Square colorful paper (15cm x 15cm)","Chunky wax crayons","Shallow plastic trays","Soapy water with blue food coloring","Small squeaky toy animals","Colorful kitchen sponges cut into fun shapes","Drinking straws"],"Reflection":"What funny sound did your animal friend make when the bubbles tickled their toes? What was your boat\\u0027s favorite dance move today?","Environment":"Indoor / Outdoor","MagicMoment":"The explosive laughter when the blue bubbles grow so tall they spill over the tray and land on the children\\u0027s noses, giving them instant \\u0027bubble mustaches\\u0027!","GroupSizeMax":10,"GroupSizeMin":4,"Accomplishment":"Successfully rescuing their animal buddy from the tickle-storm and giving their partner a high-five using a squishy, wet sponge!","ExecutionGuide":{"Ask":"What silly sound does your animal buddy make when a bubble tickles their tummy, and what is the name of your boat\\u0027s favorite dance move?","Try":"Try holding your crayon like a magic wand and scribble-scribbling as fast as a zooming rocket to make your boat\\u0027s shiny wax armor super-strong!","Watch":"Watch for silly sailors who might try to sip the soapy bubble juice through their straws; playfully show them how to blow \\u0027birthday candle\\u0027 winds OUT, and keep an eye out for ultra-soggy paper bottoms that need extra crayon scribbles!","Phases":[{"Name":"The Scribble-Race Frenzy","ChildrenDo":"Scribble-color the bottom of their paper boat as fast as they can with wax crayons to make it waterproof.","TeacherDoes":"Plays fast, goofy circus music and calls out silly coloring styles: \\u0027Color like a hyper monkey! Color like a slow-motion sloth!\\u0027","DurationMinutes":7},{"Name":"The Bubble-Pop Circus","ChildrenDo":"Place their squeaky toy in their boat, set it in the water tray, and blow through their straws to create a giant, foaming mountain of blue bubbles to float their boat to the sponge island.","TeacherDoes":"Leads a dramatic \\u0027bubble-blowing countdown\\u0027 and cheers loudly as the bubbles grow, pointing out who has the tallest bubble mountain or the best bubble mustache.","DurationMinutes":13},{"Name":"Silly Captain Parade","ChildrenDo":"Fold their paper into a simple boat shape, place it on their heads like a funny hat, and march in place making goofy engine noises.","TeacherDoes":"Guides the folding using silly names for the folds (\\u0027hot dog fold\\u0027, \\u0027bouncy triangle fold\\u0027) and snaps imaginary silly photos of the children\\u0027s hat styles.","DurationMinutes":5}],"Safety":["Remind children continuously to only blow OUT, never suck IN through the straws.","Keep plenty of dry towels handy to mop up any slippery soapy splashes on the floor immediately."],"Closing":"Lead all captains in parking their boats, giving their squeaky toys a warm towel-blanket tuck-in, and doing a giant group \\u0027Wobbly Seaweed Dance\\u0027 to celebrate their success!","Extensions":["Have a \\u0027Bubble Nose-Pop\\u0027 game where kids try to pop the tallest bubble using only the tip of their nose without touching it with their hands!","Add a drop of red paint to the sponge islands to watch the blue bubble water magically swirl into purple when they arrive!"],"Adaptations":["For younger children, pre-fold the boats so they can jump straight into the coloring and bubble-blowing play.","For older kids, challenge them to build a \\u0027bubble bridge\\u0027 across the tray using two straws at the same time."],"Preparation":["Mix water, blue food coloring, and plenty of dish soap in the plastic trays.","Cut colorful sponges into star, cloud, or heart shapes to act as \\u0027Silly Sponge Islands\\u0027 and place them inside the trays."],"MaterialSetup":["Place crayons in bright baskets, stack the square paper, and cover the water trays with colorful towels to make the \\u0027Big Bubble Reveal\\u0027 exciting."],"EnvironmentSetup":["Create a \\u0027Silly Shipyard\\u0027 coloring table with bright decorations and a nearby \\u0027Bubbly Ocean Arena\\u0027 for the water play trays."],"TeacherIntroduction":"Welcome to the Bubbly Scribble-Ship Circus! I am your Ringleader! A giant, ticklish Bubble Monster is tickling our toes! We need to make shiny, crayon-armored circus boats, grab our squeakiest animal friends, and blow a huge, wobbly shield of blue bubbles to protect them! Who is ready to get silly?","LittleMomentOpportunity":"The pure joy when a child successfully blows a bubble dome so big that it completely encapsulates their little toy animal passenger, leading to gasps and giggles.","SuggestedDurationMinutes":25},"TeacherGuidance":"Become a cartoon character! Wear a silly hat, use funny sound effects (whoosh, pop, boing), make giant cartoonish facial expressions, and treat every step like an exciting, playful game.","DevelopmentalGoals":[]}	Free	0.00	INR	Published	CuratedLicensed	1	93de0449-60c9-43ca-8a3f-5ae6a134b8d4	af2aea60-1dbc-4b11-9cbb-056ee1c0d3a6	3a48a470-63cd-492c-ba6f-8dd3032205cf	20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001	\N	2026-10-15 21:59:12.318307+00	2026-10-15 22:09:26.522776+00
009ed10c-1cb3-4275-987c-d039b6658272	Exploring Playing With Colorful Dough: Creative Tactile Studio (Focus: Make It More Playful)	Children engage in open-ended creative construction and tactile exploration centered on Playing with colorful dough. Adapted with emphasis on: Make it more playful.	Early Childhood	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	{"AgeMax":5,"AgeMin":3,"Create":"A tangible collaborative model or collage.","Together":"Children share building materials and describe what they are making to their peers.","Challenge":"Can we design and build a display inspired by Playing with colorful dough? Challenge adaptation: Make it more playful.","Materials":["Cardstock","Washable craft adhesive","Wooden craft sticks","Textured paper scraps"],"Reflection":"What was your favorite texture or tool you used while exploring Playing with colorful dough?","Environment":"Indoor / Outdoor","MagicMoment":"Noticing how different materials join together to form a new creation.","GroupSizeMax":10,"GroupSizeMin":4,"Accomplishment":"Presenting their completed project during reflection circle.","ExecutionGuide":{"Ask":"How does that piece feel when you touch it?","Try":"Try connecting two different shapes together.","Watch":"Observe hand-eye coordination and peer turn-taking.","Phases":[{"Name":"Welcome \\u0026 Material Touch","ChildrenDo":"Feel materials and select initial pieces","TeacherDoes":"Demonstrates gentle handling and asks open questions","DurationMinutes":5},{"Name":"Hands-On Creation","ChildrenDo":"Assemble and combine elements","TeacherDoes":"Circulates, providing positive reinforcement","DurationMinutes":15},{"Name":"Sharing \\u0026 Clean-Up","ChildrenDo":"Place finished crafts on drying rack and tidy up","TeacherDoes":"Leads a gentle closing transition","DurationMinutes":5}],"Safety":["Ensure only child-safe non-toxic adhesive is used","Remind children that materials remain on the table"],"Closing":"Gather on the carpet for a quick proud celebration of everyone\\u0027s work.","Extensions":["Take photos of finished structures to create a classroom storybook"],"Adaptations":["Provide larger chunky pieces for developing fine-motor grip"],"Preparation":["Cut paper into varied shapes","Set out trays on low work tables"],"MaterialSetup":["Place trays evenly within reach of small groups"],"EnvironmentSetup":["Spacious floor or craft table with accessible trays"],"TeacherIntroduction":"Today we are exploring Playing with colorful dough! Look at all these interesting textures we can build with.","LittleMomentOpportunity":"Praise a child who noticed an interesting detail in their friend\\u0027s project.","SuggestedDurationMinutes":25},"TeacherGuidance":"Introduce materials at the low table. Encourage children to test how pieces fit together.","DevelopmentalGoals":[]}	IncludedInSubscription	0.00	INR	Draft	CuratedLicensed	1	3575d272-a147-44c2-b12d-20b4e3fdc4ab	65a86559-8f85-4701-b929-f09f012b2e90	1dbd0fad-024a-49d3-a05f-ec326397f60f	20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001	\N	2026-10-17 11:38:21.181259+00	2026-10-17 11:38:21.18126+00
